window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b058-240ad9f3cdabb20a.json"]={sha256:"240ad9f3cdabb20ad3649a4ff6719fa14d0eff6f3ea09cc93541e22330a5ab9d",value:{"id":"b058","title":"橋梁動態荷重試驗","titleEn":"Dynamic bridge load testing","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"從車輛動力效應與人群同步振動出發，說明試驗載重與預期反應的計算、儀器與取樣率、趟次矩陣與封橋安全、強迫振動與人群試驗、動力放大與頻率判讀、以試驗修正係數更新評等，以及舒適度改善與基準交接，並以倫敦千禧橋的人群試驗與阻尼改造、雪梨港灣大橋 1932 年的機車載重試驗與 1940 年塔科馬海峽橋為對照。","summaryEn":"Starting from vehicle dynamic effects and crowd lock-in, explain how to compute test loads and expected responses, choose instruments and sampling rates, plan run matrices and safe closures, run forced-vibration and crowd tests, interpret amplification and frequency, update load ratings with test adjustment factors, and handle comfort retrofits and baseline handover, drawing on the crowd tests and damper retrofit of London's Millennium Bridge, the 1932 locomotive load test of Sydney Harbour Bridge and the 1940 Tacoma Narrows Bridge.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-bridge-durability-monitoring","subcategoryTitle":"橋梁耐久、檢測與健康監測","subcategoryTitleEn":"Bridge durability, inspection and health monitoring","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-bridge-durability-monitoring","learningTags":["structures","st-bridge-durability-monitoring","survey"],"architectureFamily":"survey","architectureNodes":[["試驗目的與預測反應","Test objectives and predicted response"],["試驗車輛、人群與激振器","Test trucks, crowds and shakers"],["感測器與資料擷取","Sensors and data acquisition"],["動力放大與模態判讀","Amplification and modal interpretation"],["評等修正與舒適度決策","Rating adjustment and comfort decisions"],["試驗基準與交接","Test baseline and handover"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[0,2]],"diagram":{"type":"survey","labels":["試驗目的與預測反應","試驗車輛、人群與激振器","感測器與資料擷取","動力放大與模態判讀","評等修正與舒適度決策"],"labelsEn":["Test objectives and predicted response","Test trucks, crowds and shakers","Sensors and data acquisition","Amplification and modal interpretation","Rating adjustment and comfort decisions"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：一座 30 m 簡支鋼—混凝土組合梁橋，以 300 kN 試驗車做動態試驗。(1) 預測：M = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m，最受力主梁分配 0.6 為 1,350 kN·m，S = 0.045 m³，σ = 30 MPa，ε_c = 150 με。(2) 實測：慢速峰值 ε_T = 120 με，80 km/h 三趟峰值的動力放大為 1.18、1.22、1.15，平均 1.183，95% 上限約 1.27，低於規範 1.33。(3) 頻率：模型 f = (π/2L²)√(EI/m) ≈ 4.51 Hz，實測 4.80 Hz，勁度比約 1.13。(4) 評等：K_a = 150/120 − 1 = 0.25，K_b 取 0.5，K = 1.125，RF 由 0.92 提升至約 1.04。(5) 若改變一個輸入：伸縮縫出現高差，使 80 km/h 峰值升為 168 με，DAF = 168/120 = 1.40，已超過規範的 1.33，這時不但不能以實測值放寬評等，還應先修復伸縮縫再重新試驗。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際橋梁。","textEn":"Design exercise: a 30 m simply supported steel–concrete composite girder bridge is tested dynamically with a 300 kN truck. (1) Prediction: M = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m, 0.6 of it to the most loaded girder gives 1,350 kN·m, S = 0.045 m³, σ = 30 MPa and ε_c = 150 με. (2) Measurement: the crawl peak is ε_T = 120 με, and three 80 km/h runs give amplifications of 1.18, 1.22 and 1.15, mean 1.183 and 95% upper bound about 1.27, below the code's 1.33. (3) Frequency: the model gives f = (π/2L²)√(EI/m) ≈ 4.51 Hz, the test 4.80 Hz, a stiffness ratio of about 1.13. (4) Rating: K_a = 150/120 − 1 = 0.25, K_b = 0.5, K = 1.125, so RF rises from 0.92 to about 1.04. (5) Changing one input: if a step develops at the expansion joint and the 80 km/h peak rises to 168 με, DAF = 168/120 = 1.40, above the code's 1.33, so the measured value cannot relax the rating and the joint should be repaired and the bridge retested first. Values are teaching assumptions, not any real bridge.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b058-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「車輛動力效應與衝擊係數」與「人群誘發振動與同步效應」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Vehicle dynamic effects and impact allowance\" and \"Crowd-induced vibration and lock-in\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b058-v13-01","title":"車輛動力效應與衝擊係數：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Vehicle dynamic effects and impact allowance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「動力放大係數」如何影響橋梁動態荷重試驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dynamic amplification factor” governs force, deformation or durability in “Dynamic bridge load testing”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"車輛以速度通過橋梁時，橋面不平整、伸縮縫高差與車輛懸吊的彈跳，會使橋梁反應高於同一部車緩慢通過時的靜態反應。設計規範以固定的動力載重容許值涵蓋這個效應，AASHTO 對設計車輛的靜態活載效應增加 33%；TRB 的橋梁載重試驗入門指出這個值常偏保守，主要受引道不平與伸縮縫控制。動態荷重試驗的第一個目的，就是用同一部試驗車在慢速與不同車速下的反應比值，量出這座橋實際的動力放大。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「動力放大係數」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When a vehicle crosses at speed, deck roughness, steps at expansion joints and the bounce of the vehicle suspension make the bridge respond more than when the same vehicle crawls across. Design codes cover this with a fixed dynamic load allowance; AASHTO adds 33% to the static live-load effects of the design vehicle, and the TRB primer on bridge load testing notes that this value is often conservative and is governed mainly by approach roughness and expansion joints. The first purpose of a dynamic load test is to measure this bridge's actual amplification from the ratio of responses to the same test truck at crawl speed and at various speeds. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Dynamic amplification factor” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：DAF = R_dyn/R_static。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: DAF = R_dyn/R_static.","failure":"常見誤解：「車速越快，橋梁的動力放大一定越大。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The faster the vehicle, the larger the dynamic amplification must be.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「動力放大係數」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Dynamic amplification factor”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-01-k1","title":"車輛動力效應與衝擊係數","titleEn":"Vehicle dynamic effects and impact allowance","text":"車輛以速度通過橋梁時，橋面不平整、伸縮縫高差與車輛懸吊的彈跳，會使橋梁反應高於同一部車緩慢通過時的靜態反應。設計規範以固定的動力載重容許值涵蓋這個效應，AASHTO 對設計車輛的靜態活載效應增加 33%；TRB 的橋梁載重試驗入門指出這個值常偏保守，主要受引道不平與伸縮縫控制。","textEn":"When a vehicle crosses at speed, deck roughness, steps at expansion joints and the bounce of the vehicle suspension make the bridge respond more than when the same vehicle crawls across. Design codes cover this with a fixed dynamic load allowance; AASHTO adds 33% to the static live-load effects of the design vehicle, and the TRB primer on bridge load testing notes that this value is often conservative and is governed mainly by approach roughness and expansion joints.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：車速越快，橋梁的動力放大一定越大。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The faster the vehicle, the larger the dynamic amplification must be. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「車輛動力效應與衝擊係數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Vehicle dynamic effects and impact allowance\" is correct?","options":["車速越快，橋梁的動力放大一定越大。","車輛以速度通過橋梁時，橋面不平整、伸縮縫高差與車輛懸吊的彈跳，會使橋梁反應高於同一部車緩慢通過時的靜態反應。","只要垂直頻率避開 2 Hz，人行橋就不會有振動問題。"],"optionsEn":["The faster the vehicle, the larger the dynamic amplification must be.","When a vehicle crosses at speed, deck roughness, steps at expansion joints and the bounce of the vehicle suspension make the bridge respond more than when the same vehicle crawls across.","As long as the vertical frequency avoids 2 Hz, a footbridge will have no vibration problems."],"answer":1,"explanation":"車輛以速度通過橋梁時，橋面不平整、伸縮縫高差與車輛懸吊的彈跳，會使橋梁反應高於同一部車緩慢通過時的靜態反應。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When a vehicle crosses at speed, deck roughness, steps at expansion joints and the bounce of the vehicle suspension make the bridge respond more than when the same vehicle crawls across. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b058-v13-02","title":"車輛動力效應與衝擊係數：定量估算","titleEn":"Vehicle dynamic effects and impact allowance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「動力放大係數」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dynamic amplification factor” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：DAF = R_dyn/R_static。某主梁下翼板在試驗車以低於 8 km/h 慢速通過時量得 100 με，以 70 km/h 通過時峰值 118 με：DAF = 118/100 = 1.18，即衝擊 18%，低於規範的 33%；若伸縮縫出現 20 mm 高差使峰值升為 140 με，DAF 變為 1.40。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: DAF = R_dyn/R_static. A girder bottom flange reads 100 με when the test truck crawls below 8 km/h and peaks at 118 με at 70 km/h, so DAF = 118/100 = 1.18, an impact of 18%, below the code's 33%; if a 20 mm step at an expansion joint raises the peak to 140 με, DAF becomes 1.40. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每個車速至少重複三趟，以同一車道、同一量測點的慢速平均值作為分母；確認動態峰值不是電氣雜訊或單一突波，並記錄當時橋面與伸縮縫狀況，使衝擊值能對應到具體的路面條件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Repeat each speed at least three times and use the crawl-speed average for the same lane and gauge as the denominator; confirm that dynamic peaks are not electrical noise or single spikes, and record deck and joint condition at the time so the measured impact is tied to a specific surface condition.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"DAF = R_dyn/R_static。某主梁下翼板在試驗車以低於 8 km/h 慢速通過時量得 100 με，以 70 km/h 通過時峰值 118 με：DAF = 118/100 = 1.18，即衝擊 18%，低於規範的 33%；若伸縮縫出現 20 mm 高差使峰值升為 140 με，DAF 變為 1.40。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"DAF = R_dyn/R_static. A girder bottom flange reads 100 με when the test truck crawls below 8 km/h and peaks at 118 με at 70 km/h, so DAF = 118/100 = 1.18, an impact of 18%, below the code's 33%; if a 20 mm step at an expansion joint raises the peak to 140 με, DAF becomes 1.40. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「車輛動力效應與衝擊係數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Vehicle dynamic effects and impact allowance\", which statement holds?","options":["只要量到最大應變，取樣率高低並不重要。","人行橋只要強度設計通過，就不必做人群振動試驗。","DAF = R_dyn/R_static。"],"optionsEn":["As long as the maximum strain is captured, sampling rate does not matter.","If a footbridge passes its strength design, it needs no crowd vibration test.","DAF = R_dyn/R_static."],"answer":2,"explanation":"DAF = R_dyn/R_static。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"DAF = R_dyn/R_static. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b058-v13-03","title":"車輛動力效應與衝擊係數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Vehicle dynamic effects and impact allowance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「動力放大係數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dynamic amplification factor” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每個車速至少重複三趟，以同一車道、同一量測點的慢速平均值作為分母；確認動態峰值不是電氣雜訊或單一突波，並記錄當時橋面與伸縮縫狀況，使衝擊值能對應到具體的路面條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Repeat each speed at least three times and use the crawl-speed average for the same lane and gauge as the denominator; confirm that dynamic peaks are not electrical noise or single spikes, and record deck and joint condition at the time so the measured impact is tied to a specific surface condition. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：試驗報告要寫明實測動力放大適用的路面與伸縮縫條件，並規定伸縮縫更換、路面重鋪或出現明顯高差時須重新評估；以實測值取代規範值須由評等工程師簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: The test report must state the surface and joint conditions under which the measured amplification applies, and require reassessment after joint replacement, resurfacing or a visible step; replacing the code value with a measured one needs the rating engineer's signature.","failure":"注意干擾：若只在路面剛重鋪後做試驗，量到的動力放大偏低；數年後伸縮縫磨損、引道沉陷，實際衝擊可能遠超過試驗值，以此低值放寬評等的橋就失去了原本由規範值提供的保守度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Testing only just after resurfacing measures low amplification; years later, with worn joints and settled approaches, actual impact can far exceed the test value, and a bridge whose rating was relaxed on that low value has lost the margin the code value provided. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每個車速至少重複三趟，以同一車道、同一量測點的慢速平均值作為分母；確認動態峰值不是電氣雜訊或單一突波，並記錄當時橋面與伸縮縫狀況，使衝擊值能對應到具體的路面條件。","textEn":"Repeat each speed at least three times and use the crawl-speed average for the same lane and gauge as the denominator; confirm that dynamic peaks are not electrical noise or single spikes, and record deck and joint condition at the time so the measured impact is tied to a specific surface condition.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"試驗報告要寫明實測動力放大適用的路面與伸縮縫條件，並規定伸縮縫更換、路面重鋪或出現明顯高差時須重新評估；以實測值取代規範值須由評等工程師簽認。","textEn":"The test report must state the surface and joint conditions under which the measured amplification applies, and require reassessment after joint replacement, resurfacing or a visible step; replacing the code value with a measured one needs the rating engineer's signature.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「車輛動力效應與衝擊係數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Vehicle dynamic effects and impact allowance\"?","options":["每個車速至少重複三趟，以同一車道、同一量測點的慢速平均值作為分母。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","實測應變比計算低，就可以按比例直接提高橋梁的容許載重。"],"optionsEn":["Repeat each speed at least three times and use the crawl-speed average for the same lane and gauge as the denominator.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If measured strain is lower than calculated, the permitted load can be raised in direct proportion."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每個車速至少重複三趟，以同一車道、同一量測點的慢速平均值作為分母；確認動態峰值不是電氣雜訊或單一突波，並記錄當時橋面與伸縮縫狀況，使衝擊值能對應到具體的路面條件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Repeat each speed at least three times and use the crawl-speed average for the same lane and gauge as the denominator; confirm that dynamic peaks are not electrical noise or single spikes, and record deck and joint condition at the time so the measured impact is tied to a specific surface condition. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b058-v13-04","title":"車輛動力效應與衝擊係數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Vehicle dynamic effects and impact allowance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「動力放大係數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dynamic amplification factor” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只在路面剛重鋪後做試驗，量到的動力放大偏低；數年後伸縮縫磨損、引道沉陷，實際衝擊可能遠超過試驗值，以此低值放寬評等的橋就失去了原本由規範值提供的保守度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Testing only just after resurfacing measures low amplification; years later, with worn joints and settled approaches, actual impact can far exceed the test value, and a bridge whose rating was relaxed on that low value has lost the margin the code value provided. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：動態荷重試驗的第一個目的，就是用同一部試驗車在慢速與不同車速下的反應比值，量出這座橋實際的動力放大。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The first purpose of a dynamic load test is to measure this bridge's actual amplification from the ratio of responses to the same test truck at crawl speed and at various speeds.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「車速越快，橋梁的動力放大一定越大。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The faster the vehicle, the larger the dynamic amplification must be.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只在路面剛重鋪後做試驗，量到的動力放大偏低；數年後伸縮縫磨損、引道沉陷，實際衝擊可能遠超過試驗值，以此低值放寬評等的橋就失去了原本由規範值提供的保守度。","textEn":"Testing only just after resurfacing measures low amplification; years later, with worn joints and settled approaches, actual impact can far exceed the test value, and a bridge whose rating was relaxed on that low value has lost the margin the code value provided.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「車輛動力效應與衝擊係數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Vehicle dynamic effects and impact allowance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只在路面剛重鋪後做試驗，量到的動力放大偏低；數年後伸縮縫磨損、引道沉陷，實際衝擊可能遠超過試驗值，以此低值放寬評等的橋就失去了原本由規範值提供的保守度。","只要垂直頻率避開 2 Hz，人行橋就不會有振動問題。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Testing only just after resurfacing measures low amplification.","As long as the vertical frequency avoids 2 Hz, a footbridge will have no vibration problems."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只在路面剛重鋪後做試驗，量到的動力放大偏低；數年後伸縮縫磨損、引道沉陷，實際衝擊可能遠超過試驗值，以此低值放寬評等的橋就失去了原本由規範值提供的保守度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Testing only just after resurfacing measures low amplification; years later, with worn joints and settled approaches, actual impact can far exceed the test value, and a bridge whose rating was relaxed on that low value has lost the margin the code value provided. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b058-v13-05","title":"人群誘發振動與同步效應：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Crowd-induced vibration and lock-in: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「側向步頻與人群同步」如何影響橋梁動態荷重試驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lateral footfall and crowd lock-in” governs force, deformation or durability in “Dynamic bridge load testing”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"行人步行的垂直力頻率約 2 Hz，左右腳交替產生的側向力頻率只有一半，約 1 Hz。若橋的側向振態落在這個範圍且阻尼很低，橋面輕微搖晃會讓行人不自覺調整步伐去配合，側向力因而同步放大，形成正回饋。倫敦千禧橋在 2000 年 6 月 10 日開放，兩天後就因側向振動封閉；這種同步側向激振不會隨人數平滑增加，而是在人數超過臨界值時突然出現，因此一般的單人或小群試驗看不到。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「側向步頻與人群同步」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Walking produces vertical forces at about 2 Hz, while the alternating left and right steps produce lateral forces at half that, about 1 Hz. If a bridge has a lightly damped lateral mode in this range, slight sway makes pedestrians unconsciously adjust their gait to match it, so their lateral forces synchronise and grow in positive feedback. London's Millennium Bridge opened on 10 June 2000 and closed two days later because of lateral vibration; this synchronous lateral excitation does not grow smoothly with crowd size but appears suddenly once the number of people passes a critical value, so tests with one walker or a small group do not reveal it. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Lateral footfall and crowd lock-in” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：臨界人數 N_L = 8π·ζ·f·M/k，k 為每人側向力與橋面速度的比例係數。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Critical number of pedestrians N_L = 8π·ζ·f·M/k, where k relates each person's lateral force to deck velocity.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要垂直頻率避開 2 Hz，人行橋就不會有振動問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"As long as the vertical frequency avoids 2 Hz, a footbridge will have no vibration problems.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「側向步頻與人群同步」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Lateral footfall and crowd lock-in”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-05-k1","title":"人群誘發振動與同步效應","titleEn":"Crowd-induced vibration and lock-in","text":"行人步行的垂直力頻率約 2 Hz，左右腳交替產生的側向力頻率只有一半，約 1 Hz。若橋的側向振態落在這個範圍且阻尼很低，橋面輕微搖晃會讓行人不自覺調整步伐去配合，側向力因而同步放大，形成正回饋。","textEn":"Walking produces vertical forces at about 2 Hz, while the alternating left and right steps produce lateral forces at half that, about 1 Hz. If a bridge has a lightly damped lateral mode in this range, slight sway makes pedestrians unconsciously adjust their gait to match it, so their lateral forces synchronise and grow in positive feedback.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要垂直頻率避開 2 Hz，人行橋就不會有振動問題。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: As long as the vertical frequency avoids 2 Hz, a footbridge will have no vibration problems. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「人群誘發振動與同步效應」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Crowd-induced vibration and lock-in\" is correct?","options":["只要垂直頻率避開 2 Hz，人行橋就不會有振動問題。","載重試驗用的車越重，得到的結論就越可靠。","行人步行的垂直力頻率約 2 Hz，左右腳交替產生的側向力頻率只有一半，約 1 Hz。"],"optionsEn":["As long as the vertical frequency avoids 2 Hz, a footbridge will have no vibration problems.","The heavier the test vehicle, the more reliable the conclusions.","Walking produces vertical forces at about 2 Hz, while the alternating left and right steps produce lateral forces at half that, about 1 Hz."],"answer":2,"explanation":"行人步行的垂直力頻率約 2 Hz，左右腳交替產生的側向力頻率只有一半，約 1 Hz。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Walking produces vertical forces at about 2 Hz, while the alternating left and right steps produce lateral forces at half that, about 1 Hz. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b058-v13-06","title":"人群誘發振動與同步效應：定量估算","titleEn":"Crowd-induced vibration and lock-in: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「側向步頻與人群同步」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lateral footfall and crowd lock-in” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：臨界人數 N_L = 8π·ζ·f·M/k，k 為每人側向力與橋面速度的比例係數。取 ζ = 0.7%、f = 1.0 Hz、模態質量 M = 130,000 kg、k = 300 N·s/m：N_L = 8π×0.007×1.0×130,000/300 ≈ 76 人；阻尼提高到 15% 時 N_L ≈ 1,630 人。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Critical number of pedestrians N_L = 8π·ζ·f·M/k, where k relates each person's lateral force to deck velocity. With ζ = 0.7%, f = 1.0 Hz, modal mass M = 130,000 kg and k = 300 N·s/m, N_L = 8π×0.007×1.0×130,000/300 ≈ 76 people; raising damping to 15% gives N_L ≈ 1,630 people. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以逐步增加人數的群眾步行試驗，同步量測橋面側向加速度與橋上人數，找出加速度突然非線性增加時的人數，並與 N_L 估計比較；試驗須設定中止準則，例如側向加速度超過預定值即停止放行並疏散。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run walking tests with stepwise increases in crowd size while measuring lateral deck acceleration and the number on the bridge, find the count at which acceleration suddenly grows nonlinearly and compare it with the N_L estimate; set a stop criterion, for example halting entry and clearing the deck once lateral acceleration exceeds a preset value.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"臨界人數 N_L = 8π·ζ·f·M/k，k 為每人側向力與橋面速度的比例係數。取 ζ = 0.7%、f = 1.0 Hz、模態質量 M = 130,000 kg、k = 300 N·s/m：N_L = 8π×0.007×1.0×130,000/300 ≈ 76 人；阻尼提高到 15% 時 N_L ≈ 1,630 人。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Critical number of pedestrians N_L = 8π·ζ·f·M/k, where k relates each person's lateral force to deck velocity. With ζ = 0.7%, f = 1.0 Hz, modal mass M = 130,000 kg and k = 300 N·s/m, N_L = 8π×0.007×1.0×130,000/300 ≈ 76 people; raising damping to 15% gives N_L ≈ 1,630 people. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「人群誘發振動與同步效應」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Crowd-induced vibration and lock-in\", which statement holds?","options":["臨界人數 N_L = 8π·ζ·f·M/k，k 為每人側向力與橋面速度的比例係數。","動態試驗只要讓卡車以最高速通過一次就夠了。","實測頻率比模型高，就代表橋梁沒有任何問題。"],"optionsEn":["Critical number of pedestrians N_L = 8π·ζ·f·M/k, where k relates each person's lateral force to deck velocity.","A dynamic test only needs one pass of the truck at top speed.","A measured frequency higher than the model means the bridge has no problems."],"answer":0,"explanation":"臨界人數 N_L = 8π·ζ·f·M/k，k 為每人側向力與橋面速度的比例係數。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Critical number of pedestrians N_L = 8π·ζ·f·M/k, where k relates each person's lateral force to deck velocity. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b058-v13-07","title":"人群誘發振動與同步效應：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Crowd-induced vibration and lock-in: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「側向步頻與人群同步」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lateral footfall and crowd lock-in” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以逐步增加人數的群眾步行試驗，同步量測橋面側向加速度與橋上人數，找出加速度突然非線性增加時的人數，並與 N_L 估計比較；試驗須設定中止準則，例如側向加速度超過預定值即停止放行並疏散。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run walking tests with stepwise increases in crowd size while measuring lateral deck acceleration and the number on the bridge, find the count at which acceleration suddenly grows nonlinearly and compare it with the N_L estimate; set a stop criterion, for example halting entry and clearing the deck once lateral acceleration exceeds a preset value. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：人行橋設計須同時檢查垂直與側向振態；側向頻率低於約 1.3 Hz 且質量輕時，要以人群密度情境評估同步風險，並預留加裝阻尼器的空間與連接點，開放前由設計者主持人群試驗並簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Check both vertical and lateral modes in footbridge design; where a light deck has lateral frequencies below about 1.3 Hz, assess lock-in risk under crowd-density scenarios and reserve space and connections for dampers, with a crowd test led and signed off by the designer before opening.","failure":"注意干擾：千禧橋開幕日約有 90,000 人通過、同時最多約 2,000 人在橋上，側向擺動最大約 70 mm，行人需要扶著欄杆行走；橋梁開放兩天即封閉，改造工程自 2001 年 5 月持續到 2002 年 1 月。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: On the Millennium Bridge's opening day about 90,000 people crossed with up to about 2,000 on the deck at once; lateral sway reached about 70 mm and walkers had to hold the handrails. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以逐步增加人數的群眾步行試驗，同步量測橋面側向加速度與橋上人數，找出加速度突然非線性增加時的人數，並與 N_L 估計比較；試驗須設定中止準則，例如側向加速度超過預定值即停止放行並疏散。","textEn":"Run walking tests with stepwise increases in crowd size while measuring lateral deck acceleration and the number on the bridge, find the count at which acceleration suddenly grows nonlinearly and compare it with the N_L estimate; set a stop criterion, for example halting entry and clearing the deck once lateral acceleration exceeds a preset value.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"人行橋設計須同時檢查垂直與側向振態；側向頻率低於約 1.3 Hz 且質量輕時，要以人群密度情境評估同步風險，並預留加裝阻尼器的空間與連接點，開放前由設計者主持人群試驗並簽認。","textEn":"Check both vertical and lateral modes in footbridge design; where a light deck has lateral frequencies below about 1.3 Hz, assess lock-in risk under crowd-density scenarios and reserve space and connections for dampers, with a crowd test led and signed off by the designer before opening.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「人群誘發振動與同步效應」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Crowd-induced vibration and lock-in\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以逐步增加人數的群眾步行試驗，同步量測橋面側向加速度與橋上人數，找出加速度突然非線性增加時的人數，並與 N_L 估計比較。","加大構件斷面一定是解決人行橋振動最有效的方法。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Run walking tests with stepwise increases in crowd size while measuring lateral deck acceleration and the number on the bridge, find the count at which acceleration suddenly grows nonlinearly and compare it with the N_L estimate.","Enlarging member sections is always the most effective cure for footbridge vibration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以逐步增加人數的群眾步行試驗，同步量測橋面側向加速度與橋上人數，找出加速度突然非線性增加時的人數，並與 N_L 估計比較；試驗須設定中止準則，例如側向加速度超過預定值即停止放行並疏散。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run walking tests with stepwise increases in crowd size while measuring lateral deck acceleration and the number on the bridge, find the count at which acceleration suddenly grows nonlinearly and compare it with the N_L estimate; set a stop criterion, for example halting entry and clearing the deck once lateral acceleration exceeds a preset value. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b058-v13-08","title":"人群誘發振動與同步效應：失效診斷","titleEn":"Crowd-induced vibration and lock-in: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「側向步頻與人群同步」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lateral footfall and crowd lock-in” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"千禧橋開幕日約有 90,000 人通過、同時最多約 2,000 人在橋上，側向擺動最大約 70 mm，行人需要扶著欄杆行走；橋梁開放兩天即封閉，改造工程自 2001 年 5 月持續到 2002 年 1 月。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"On the Millennium Bridge's opening day about 90,000 people crossed with up to about 2,000 on the deck at once; lateral sway reached about 70 mm and walkers had to hold the handrails. The bridge closed after two days, and the retrofit ran from May 2001 to January 2002. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：倫敦千禧橋在 2000 年 6 月 10 日開放，兩天後就因側向振動封閉；這種同步側向激振不會隨人數平滑增加，而是在人數超過臨界值時突然出現，因此一般的單人或小群試驗看不到。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: London's Millennium Bridge opened on 10 June 2000 and closed two days later because of lateral vibration; this synchronous lateral excitation does not grow smoothly with crowd size but appears suddenly once the number of people passes a critical value, so tests with one walker or a small group do not reveal it.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要垂直頻率避開 2 Hz，人行橋就不會有振動問題。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"As long as the vertical frequency avoids 2 Hz, a footbridge will have no vibration problems.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"千禧橋開幕日約有 90,000 人通過、同時最多約 2,000 人在橋上，側向擺動最大約 70 mm，行人需要扶著欄杆行走；橋梁開放兩天即封閉，改造工程自 2001 年 5 月持續到 2002 年 1 月。","textEn":"On the Millennium Bridge's opening day about 90,000 people crossed with up to about 2,000 on the deck at once; lateral sway reached about 70 mm and walkers had to hold the handrails. The bridge closed after two days, and the retrofit ran from May 2001 to January 2002.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「人群誘發振動與同步效應」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Crowd-induced vibration and lock-in\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","載重試驗用的車越重，得到的結論就越可靠。","千禧橋開幕日約有 90,000 人通過、同時最多約 2,000 人在橋上，側向擺動最大約 70 mm，行人需要扶著欄杆行走。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The heavier the test vehicle, the more reliable the conclusions.","On the Millennium Bridge's opening day about 90,000 people crossed with up to about 2,000 on the deck at once."],"answer":2,"explanation":"千禧橋開幕日約有 90,000 人通過、同時最多約 2,000 人在橋上，側向擺動最大約 70 mm，行人需要扶著欄杆行走；橋梁開放兩天即封閉，改造工程自 2001 年 5 月持續到 2002 年 1 月。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"On the Millennium Bridge's opening day about 90,000 people crossed with up to about 2,000 on the deck at once; lateral sway reached about 70 mm and walkers had to hold the handrails. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b058-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「試驗載重與預期反應」與「量測儀器與取樣率」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Test loads and predicted response\" and \"Instrumentation and sampling rate\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b058-v13-09","title":"試驗載重與預期反應：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Test loads and predicted response: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「試驗車輛軸重」如何影響橋梁動態荷重試驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Test-vehicle axle weights” governs force, deformation or durability in “Dynamic bridge load testing”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"試驗載重必須是已知的：每部試驗車都要以地磅逐軸秤重並量測軸距，裝載物固定不可移動，量測反應才能與計算比較。1932 年雪梨港灣大橋開放前，以最多 96 部蒸汽機車頭尾相接排滿四條鐵軌，進行約三週的載重試驗後才宣布安全，那是以極大靜載驗證整體行為的做法。動態試驗的載重較輕，卻更重視可重複性：同一部車、同一車道、不同車速，並以事先計算的預期反應決定感測器量程與停止準則。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「試驗車輛軸重」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The test load must be known: each test vehicle is weighed axle by axle on a weighbridge and its axle spacing measured, with the payload secured so that measured responses can be compared with calculations. Before Sydney Harbour Bridge opened in 1932, up to 96 steam locomotives were placed end to end across its four rail tracks for about three weeks of testing before it was declared safe, a verification of overall behaviour with a very large static load. Dynamic tests use lighter loads but care more about repeatability: the same truck, the same lane, different speeds, with predicted responses computed beforehand to set sensor ranges and stop criteria. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Test-vehicle axle weights” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：30 m 簡支梁跨中，300 kN 試驗車近似集中載重：M = PL/4 = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m；分配到最受力主梁 0.6 倍為 1,350 kN·m，斷面模數 S = 0.045 m³：σ = 1.35×10⁶ N·m/0.045 m³ = 30 MPa，鋼材 ε = 30/200,000 = 150 με。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a 30 m simple span with a 300 kN test truck approximated as a midspan point load, M = PL/4 = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m; distributing 0.6 of it to the most loaded girder gives 1,350 kN·m, and with section modulus S = 0.045 m³, σ = 1.35×10⁶ N·m/0.045 m³ = 30 MPa, a steel strain of ε = 30/200,000 = 150 με.","failure":"常見誤解：「載重試驗用的車越重，得到的結論就越可靠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The heavier the test vehicle, the more reliable the conclusions.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「試驗車輛軸重」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Test-vehicle axle weights”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-09-k1","title":"試驗載重與預期反應","titleEn":"Test loads and predicted response","text":"試驗載重必須是已知的：每部試驗車都要以地磅逐軸秤重並量測軸距，裝載物固定不可移動，量測反應才能與計算比較。1932 年雪梨港灣大橋開放前，以最多 96 部蒸汽機車頭尾相接排滿四條鐵軌，進行約三週的載重試驗後才宣布安全，那是以極大靜載驗證整體行為的做法。","textEn":"The test load must be known: each test vehicle is weighed axle by axle on a weighbridge and its axle spacing measured, with the payload secured so that measured responses can be compared with calculations. Before Sydney Harbour Bridge opened in 1932, up to 96 steam locomotives were placed end to end across its four rail tracks for about three weeks of testing before it was declared safe, a verification of overall behaviour with a very large static load.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：載重試驗用的車越重，得到的結論就越可靠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The heavier the test vehicle, the more reliable the conclusions. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「試驗載重與預期反應」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Test loads and predicted response\" is correct?","options":["試驗載重必須是已知的：每部試驗車都要以地磅逐軸秤重並量測軸距，裝載物固定不可移動，量測反應才能與計算比較。","載重試驗用的車越重，得到的結論就越可靠。","只要量到最大應變，取樣率高低並不重要。"],"optionsEn":["The test load must be known: each test vehicle is weighed axle by axle on a weighbridge and its axle spacing measured, with the payload secured so that measured responses can be compared with calculations.","The heavier the test vehicle, the more reliable the conclusions.","As long as the maximum strain is captured, sampling rate does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"試驗載重必須是已知的：每部試驗車都要以地磅逐軸秤重並量測軸距，裝載物固定不可移動，量測反應才能與計算比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The test load must be known: each test vehicle is weighed axle by axle on a weighbridge and its axle spacing measured, with the payload secured so that measured responses can be compared with calculations. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b058-v13-10","title":"試驗載重與預期反應：定量估算","titleEn":"Test loads and predicted response: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「試驗車輛軸重」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Test-vehicle axle weights” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：30 m 簡支梁跨中，300 kN 試驗車近似集中載重：M = PL/4 = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m；分配到最受力主梁 0.6 倍為 1,350 kN·m，斷面模數 S = 0.045 m³：σ = 1.35×10⁶ N·m/0.045 m³ = 30 MPa，鋼材 ε = 30/200,000 = 150 με。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a 30 m simple span with a 300 kN test truck approximated as a midspan point load, M = PL/4 = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m; distributing 0.6 of it to the most loaded girder gives 1,350 kN·m, and with section modulus S = 0.045 m³, σ = 1.35×10⁶ N·m/0.045 m³ = 30 MPa, a steel strain of ε = 30/200,000 = 150 με. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：試驗前由第三方地磅出具逐軸重量與總重證明，量測軸距與輪距並拍照；以實際數值重算影響線反應，訂出每個量測點的預期值與停止門檻，例如預期值的 1.2 倍或規範容許應力的一定比例。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before testing, obtain third-party weighbridge tickets for each axle and the gross weight, measure and photograph axle and wheel spacing, recompute influence-line responses with the actual values, and set an expected value and stop threshold for each gauge, for example 1.2 times the prediction or a set fraction of the allowable stress.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"30 m 簡支梁跨中，300 kN 試驗車近似集中載重：M = PL/4 = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m；分配到最受力主梁 0.6 倍為 1,350 kN·m，斷面模數 S = 0.045 m³：σ = 1.35×10⁶ N·m/0.045 m³ = 30 MPa，鋼材 ε = 30/200,000 = 150 με。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a 30 m simple span with a 300 kN test truck approximated as a midspan point load, M = PL/4 = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m; distributing 0.6 of it to the most loaded girder gives 1,350 kN·m, and with section modulus S = 0.045 m³, σ = 1.35×10⁶ N·m/0.045 m³ = 30 MPa, a steel strain of ε = 30/200,000 = 150 με. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「試驗載重與預期反應」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Test loads and predicted response\", which statement holds?","options":["人行橋只要強度設計通過，就不必做人群振動試驗。","30 m 簡支梁跨中，300 kN 試驗車近似集中載重：M = PL/4 = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m。","實測應變比計算低，就可以按比例直接提高橋梁的容許載重。"],"optionsEn":["If a footbridge passes its strength design, it needs no crowd vibration test.","For a 30 m simple span with a 300 kN test truck approximated as a midspan point load, M = PL/4 = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m.","If measured strain is lower than calculated, the permitted load can be raised in direct proportion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"30 m 簡支梁跨中，300 kN 試驗車近似集中載重：M = PL/4 = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m；分配到最受力主梁 0.6 倍為 1,350 kN·m，斷面模數 S = 0.045 m³：σ = 1.35×10⁶ N·m/0.045 m³ = 30 MPa，鋼材 ε = 30/200,000 = 150 με。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a 30 m simple span with a 300 kN test truck approximated as a midspan point load, M = PL/4 = 300×30/4 = 2,250 kN·m; distributing 0.6 of it to the most loaded girder gives 1,350 kN·m, and with section modulus S = 0.045 m³, σ = 1.35×10⁶ N·m/0.045 m³ = 30 MPa, a steel strain of ε = 30/200,000 = 150 με. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b058-v13-11","title":"試驗載重與預期反應：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Test loads and predicted response: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「試驗車輛軸重」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Test-vehicle axle weights” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"試驗前由第三方地磅出具逐軸重量與總重證明，量測軸距與輪距並拍照；以實際數值重算影響線反應，訂出每個量測點的預期值與停止門檻，例如預期值的 1.2 倍或規範容許應力的一定比例。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before testing, obtain third-party weighbridge tickets for each axle and the gross weight, measure and photograph axle and wheel spacing, recompute influence-line responses with the actual values, and set an expected value and stop threshold for each gauge, for example 1.2 times the prediction or a set fraction of the allowable stress. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：試驗計畫須由評等或設計工程師核算試驗載重不超過構件容許值，列出逐級加載與停止準則；試驗當天現場要有有權中止試驗的工程師在場，所有決定記錄在試驗日誌。","observationEn":"Site practice: The test plan must have the rating or design engineer confirm that test loads stay within member capacities and list load stages and stop criteria; on test day an engineer with authority to stop the test must be on site, and every decision goes into the test log.","failure":"注意干擾：若試驗車載運砂石卻未秤重、只依車型估計，或試驗中途更換車輛，量測反應就無法與計算比較；試驗車過重則可能讓已劣化的構件在試驗中受損，試驗本身變成事故。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If a gravel-loaded truck is not weighed but estimated from its type, or vehicles are swapped mid-test, measured responses cannot be compared with calculations; an overweight truck can damage deteriorated members during the test, turning the test into an incident. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"試驗前由第三方地磅出具逐軸重量與總重證明，量測軸距與輪距並拍照；以實際數值重算影響線反應，訂出每個量測點的預期值與停止門檻，例如預期值的 1.2 倍或規範容許應力的一定比例。","textEn":"Before testing, obtain third-party weighbridge tickets for each axle and the gross weight, measure and photograph axle and wheel spacing, recompute influence-line responses with the actual values, and set an expected value and stop threshold for each gauge, for example 1.2 times the prediction or a set fraction of the allowable stress.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"試驗計畫須由評等或設計工程師核算試驗載重不超過構件容許值，列出逐級加載與停止準則；試驗當天現場要有有權中止試驗的工程師在場，所有決定記錄在試驗日誌。","textEn":"The test plan must have the rating or design engineer confirm that test loads stay within member capacities and list load stages and stop criteria; on test day an engineer with authority to stop the test must be on site, and every decision goes into the test log.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「試驗載重與預期反應」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Test loads and predicted response\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","載重試驗通過一次，就證明橋梁永遠安全。","試驗前由第三方地磅出具逐軸重量與總重證明，量測軸距與輪距並拍照。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Passing one load test proves the bridge safe forever.","Before testing, obtain third-party weighbridge tickets for each axle and the gross weight, measure and photograph axle and wheel spacing, recompute influence-line responses with the actual values, and set an expected value and stop threshold for each gauge, for example 1.2 times the prediction or a set fraction of the allowable stress."],"answer":2,"explanation":"試驗前由第三方地磅出具逐軸重量與總重證明，量測軸距與輪距並拍照；以實際數值重算影響線反應，訂出每個量測點的預期值與停止門檻，例如預期值的 1.2 倍或規範容許應力的一定比例。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before testing, obtain third-party weighbridge tickets for each axle and the gross weight, measure and photograph axle and wheel spacing, recompute influence-line responses with the actual values, and set an expected value and stop threshold for each gauge, for example 1.2 times the prediction or a set fraction of the allowable stress. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b058-v13-12","title":"試驗載重與預期反應：失效診斷","titleEn":"Test loads and predicted response: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「試驗車輛軸重」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Test-vehicle axle weights” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若試驗車載運砂石卻未秤重、只依車型估計，或試驗中途更換車輛，量測反應就無法與計算比較；試驗車過重則可能讓已劣化的構件在試驗中受損，試驗本身變成事故。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If a gravel-loaded truck is not weighed but estimated from its type, or vehicles are swapped mid-test, measured responses cannot be compared with calculations; an overweight truck can damage deteriorated members during the test, turning the test into an incident. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：動態試驗的載重較輕，卻更重視可重複性：同一部車、同一車道、不同車速，並以事先計算的預期反應決定感測器量程與停止準則。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Dynamic tests use lighter loads but care more about repeatability: the same truck, the same lane, different speeds, with predicted responses computed beforehand to set sensor ranges and stop criteria.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「載重試驗用的車越重，得到的結論就越可靠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The heavier the test vehicle, the more reliable the conclusions.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若試驗車載運砂石卻未秤重、只依車型估計，或試驗中途更換車輛，量測反應就無法與計算比較；試驗車過重則可能讓已劣化的構件在試驗中受損，試驗本身變成事故。","textEn":"If a gravel-loaded truck is not weighed but estimated from its type, or vehicles are swapped mid-test, measured responses cannot be compared with calculations; an overweight truck can damage deteriorated members during the test, turning the test into an incident.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「試驗載重與預期反應」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Test loads and predicted response\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若試驗車載運砂石卻未秤重、只依車型估計，或試驗中途更換車輛，量測反應就無法與計算比較；試驗車過重則可能讓已劣化的構件在試驗中受損，試驗本身變成事故。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要量到最大應變，取樣率高低並不重要。"],"optionsEn":["If a gravel-loaded truck is not weighed but estimated from its type, or vehicles are swapped mid-test, measured responses cannot be compared with calculations.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","As long as the maximum strain is captured, sampling rate does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若試驗車載運砂石卻未秤重、只依車型估計，或試驗中途更換車輛，量測反應就無法與計算比較；試驗車過重則可能讓已劣化的構件在試驗中受損，試驗本身變成事故。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If a gravel-loaded truck is not weighed but estimated from its type, or vehicles are swapped mid-test, measured responses cannot be compared with calculations; an overweight truck can damage deteriorated members during the test, turning the test into an incident. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b058-v13-13","title":"量測儀器與取樣率：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Instrumentation and sampling rate: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「動態應變計與加速度計」如何影響橋梁動態荷重試驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dynamic strain gauges and accelerometers” governs force, deformation or durability in “Dynamic bridge load testing”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"動態試驗同時需要三類資料：主梁與關鍵構件的應變、跨中撓度或加速度，以及車輛位置與速度。應變計要能反應快速變化，加速度計的頻寬與解析度要涵蓋主要振態與試驗產生的微小加速度，撓度可用線性位移計、雷射或雷達干涉儀量測。車輛位置可用路面觸發開關或影像同步，讓每一筆反應都能對應到荷重位置，這是區分靜態與動態成分的前提。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「動態應變計與加速度計」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A dynamic test needs three kinds of data at once: strains in girders and critical members, midspan deflection or acceleration, and vehicle position and speed. Strain gauges must follow fast changes, accelerometers need bandwidth and resolution covering the main modes and the small accelerations a test produces, and deflection can be measured by displacement transducers, laser or radar interferometry. Vehicle position from road-surface trigger switches or synchronised video lets every response be tied to load position, the precondition for separating static from dynamic components. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Dynamic strain gauges and accelerometers” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：試驗車以 80 km/h（22.2 m/s）通過 30 m 跨需 30/22.2 ≈ 1.35 s；若每次通過要有至少 50 個取樣點描述影響線，取樣率 ≥ 50/1.35 ≈ 37 Hz；要辨識 20 Hz 以下的振態，依 2.56 倍規則需 ≥ 51.2 Hz，因此取 100 Hz 以上。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A truck at 80 km/h (22.2 m/s) crosses a 30 m span in 30/22.2 ≈ 1.35 s; at least 50 samples per crossing to describe the influence line needs ≥ 50/1.35 ≈ 37 Hz, and identifying modes up to 20 Hz by the 2.56 rule needs ≥ 51.2 Hz, so 100 Hz or more is chosen.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要量到最大應變，取樣率高低並不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"As long as the maximum strain is captured, sampling rate does not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「動態應變計與加速度計」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Dynamic strain gauges and accelerometers”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-13-k1","title":"量測儀器與取樣率","titleEn":"Instrumentation and sampling rate","text":"動態試驗同時需要三類資料：主梁與關鍵構件的應變、跨中撓度或加速度，以及車輛位置與速度。應變計要能反應快速變化，加速度計的頻寬與解析度要涵蓋主要振態與試驗產生的微小加速度，撓度可用線性位移計、雷射或雷達干涉儀量測。","textEn":"A dynamic test needs three kinds of data at once: strains in girders and critical members, midspan deflection or acceleration, and vehicle position and speed. Strain gauges must follow fast changes, accelerometers need bandwidth and resolution covering the main modes and the small accelerations a test produces, and deflection can be measured by displacement transducers, laser or radar interferometry.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要量到最大應變，取樣率高低並不重要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: As long as the maximum strain is captured, sampling rate does not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「量測儀器與取樣率」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Instrumentation and sampling rate\" is correct?","options":["只要量到最大應變，取樣率高低並不重要。","動態試驗同時需要三類資料：主梁與關鍵構件的應變、跨中撓度或加速度，以及車輛位置與速度。","動態試驗只要讓卡車以最高速通過一次就夠了。"],"optionsEn":["As long as the maximum strain is captured, sampling rate does not matter.","A dynamic test needs three kinds of data at once: strains in girders and critical members, midspan deflection or acceleration, and vehicle position and speed.","A dynamic test only needs one pass of the truck at top speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"動態試驗同時需要三類資料：主梁與關鍵構件的應變、跨中撓度或加速度，以及車輛位置與速度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A dynamic test needs three kinds of data at once: strains in girders and critical members, midspan deflection or acceleration, and vehicle position and speed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b058-v13-14","title":"量測儀器與取樣率：定量估算","titleEn":"Instrumentation and sampling rate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「動態應變計與加速度計」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dynamic strain gauges and accelerometers” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：試驗車以 80 km/h（22.2 m/s）通過 30 m 跨需 30/22.2 ≈ 1.35 s；若每次通過要有至少 50 個取樣點描述影響線，取樣率 ≥ 50/1.35 ≈ 37 Hz；要辨識 20 Hz 以下的振態，依 2.56 倍規則需 ≥ 51.2 Hz，因此取 100 Hz 以上。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A truck at 80 km/h (22.2 m/s) crosses a 30 m span in 30/22.2 ≈ 1.35 s; at least 50 samples per crossing to describe the influence line needs ≥ 50/1.35 ≈ 37 Hz, and identifying modes up to 20 Hz by the 2.56 rule needs ≥ 51.2 Hz, so 100 Hz or more is chosen. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：試驗前檢查每個通道的方向、增益與雜訊底線，並以已知敲擊或靜置歸零確認；每一趟試驗後立即檢視資料是否飽和、缺漏或觸發錯位，有問題的趟次當場重做，而不是回辦公室才發現。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before testing, check every channel's orientation, gain and noise floor and confirm with a known tap or a static zero; after each run, inspect the data immediately for saturation, gaps or trigger misalignment and repeat faulty runs on the spot rather than discovering them back at the office.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"試驗車以 80 km/h（22.2 m/s）通過 30 m 跨需 30/22.2 ≈ 1.35 s；若每次通過要有至少 50 個取樣點描述影響線，取樣率 ≥ 50/1.35 ≈ 37 Hz；要辨識 20 Hz 以下的振態，依 2.56 倍規則需 ≥ 51.2 Hz，因此取 100 Hz 以上。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A truck at 80 km/h (22.2 m/s) crosses a 30 m span in 30/22.2 ≈ 1.35 s; at least 50 samples per crossing to describe the influence line needs ≥ 50/1.35 ≈ 37 Hz, and identifying modes up to 20 Hz by the 2.56 rule needs ≥ 51.2 Hz, so 100 Hz or more is chosen. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「量測儀器與取樣率」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Instrumentation and sampling rate\", which statement holds?","options":["實測頻率比模型高，就代表橋梁沒有任何問題。","加大構件斷面一定是解決人行橋振動最有效的方法。","試驗車以 80 km/h（22.2 m/s）通過 30 m 跨需 30/22.2 ≈ 1.35 s。"],"optionsEn":["A measured frequency higher than the model means the bridge has no problems.","Enlarging member sections is always the most effective cure for footbridge vibration.","A truck at 80 km/h (22.2 m/s) crosses a 30 m span in 30/22.2 ≈ 1.35 s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"試驗車以 80 km/h（22.2 m/s）通過 30 m 跨需 30/22.2 ≈ 1.35 s；若每次通過要有至少 50 個取樣點描述影響線，取樣率 ≥ 50/1.35 ≈ 37 Hz；要辨識 20 Hz 以下的振態，依 2.56 倍規則需 ≥ 51.2 Hz，因此取 100 Hz 以上。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A truck at 80 km/h (22.2 m/s) crosses a 30 m span in 30/22.2 ≈ 1.35 s; at least 50 samples per crossing to describe the influence line needs ≥ 50/1.35 ≈ 37 Hz, and identifying modes up to 20 Hz by the 2.56 rule needs ≥ 51.2 Hz, so 100 Hz or more is chosen. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b058-v13-15","title":"量測儀器與取樣率：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Instrumentation and sampling rate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「動態應變計與加速度計」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dynamic strain gauges and accelerometers” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"試驗前檢查每個通道的方向、增益與雜訊底線，並以已知敲擊或靜置歸零確認；每一趟試驗後立即檢視資料是否飽和、缺漏或觸發錯位，有問題的趟次當場重做，而不是回辦公室才發現。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before testing, check every channel's orientation, gain and noise floor and confirm with a known tap or a static zero; after each run, inspect the data immediately for saturation, gaps or trigger misalignment and repeat faulty runs on the spot rather than discovering them back at the office. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：量測計畫以表格列出每個通道的感測器型號、位置、方向、量程、取樣率與預期值，現場安裝後逐一拍照核對；所有通道共用同一時間基準，原始檔案保留車輛觸發訊號。","observationEn":"Site practice: The instrumentation plan tabulates sensor model, location, orientation, range, sampling rate and expected value for every channel, with each installation photographed and checked; all channels share one time base, and raw files keep the vehicle trigger signals.","failure":"注意干擾：取樣率太低時峰值被削掉，算出的動力放大偏小；位移計架在會隨橋振動的臨時支架上，量到的其實是支架的運動；車輛位置沒有同步，事後就無法判斷峰值發生時車在哪裡。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Too low a sampling rate clips peaks and underestimates amplification; a displacement transducer on a temporary frame that vibrates with the bridge measures the frame; without synchronised vehicle position nobody can later tell where the truck was at the peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"試驗前檢查每個通道的方向、增益與雜訊底線，並以已知敲擊或靜置歸零確認；每一趟試驗後立即檢視資料是否飽和、缺漏或觸發錯位，有問題的趟次當場重做，而不是回辦公室才發現。","textEn":"Before testing, check every channel's orientation, gain and noise floor and confirm with a known tap or a static zero; after each run, inspect the data immediately for saturation, gaps or trigger misalignment and repeat faulty runs on the spot rather than discovering them back at the office.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"量測計畫以表格列出每個通道的感測器型號、位置、方向、量程、取樣率與預期值，現場安裝後逐一拍照核對；所有通道共用同一時間基準，原始檔案保留車輛觸發訊號。","textEn":"The instrumentation plan tabulates sensor model, location, orientation, range, sampling rate and expected value for every channel, with each installation photographed and checked; all channels share one time base, and raw files keep the vehicle trigger signals.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「量測儀器與取樣率」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Instrumentation and sampling rate\"?","options":["試驗前檢查每個通道的方向、增益與雜訊底線，並以已知敲擊或靜置歸零確認。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","車速越快，橋梁的動力放大一定越大。"],"optionsEn":["Before testing, check every channel's orientation, gain and noise floor and confirm with a known tap or a static zero.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The faster the vehicle, the larger the dynamic amplification must be."],"answer":0,"explanation":"試驗前檢查每個通道的方向、增益與雜訊底線，並以已知敲擊或靜置歸零確認；每一趟試驗後立即檢視資料是否飽和、缺漏或觸發錯位，有問題的趟次當場重做，而不是回辦公室才發現。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before testing, check every channel's orientation, gain and noise floor and confirm with a known tap or a static zero; after each run, inspect the data immediately for saturation, gaps or trigger misalignment and repeat faulty runs on the spot rather than discovering them back at the office. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b058-v13-16","title":"量測儀器與取樣率：失效診斷","titleEn":"Instrumentation and sampling rate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「動態應變計與加速度計」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dynamic strain gauges and accelerometers” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"取樣率太低時峰值被削掉，算出的動力放大偏小；位移計架在會隨橋振動的臨時支架上，量到的其實是支架的運動；車輛位置沒有同步，事後就無法判斷峰值發生時車在哪裡。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Too low a sampling rate clips peaks and underestimates amplification; a displacement transducer on a temporary frame that vibrates with the bridge measures the frame; without synchronised vehicle position nobody can later tell where the truck was at the peak. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：車輛位置可用路面觸發開關或影像同步，讓每一筆反應都能對應到荷重位置，這是區分靜態與動態成分的前提。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Vehicle position from road-surface trigger switches or synchronised video lets every response be tied to load position, the precondition for separating static from dynamic components.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要量到最大應變，取樣率高低並不重要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"As long as the maximum strain is captured, sampling rate does not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"取樣率太低時峰值被削掉，算出的動力放大偏小；位移計架在會隨橋振動的臨時支架上，量到的其實是支架的運動；車輛位置沒有同步，事後就無法判斷峰值發生時車在哪裡。","textEn":"Too low a sampling rate clips peaks and underestimates amplification; a displacement transducer on a temporary frame that vibrates with the bridge measures the frame; without synchronised vehicle position nobody can later tell where the truck was at the peak.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「量測儀器與取樣率」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Instrumentation and sampling rate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","取樣率太低時峰值被削掉，算出的動力放大偏小；位移計架在會隨橋振動的臨時支架上，量到的其實是支架的運動；車輛位置沒有同步，事後就無法判斷峰值發生時車在哪裡。","動態試驗只要讓卡車以最高速通過一次就夠了。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Too low a sampling rate clips peaks and underestimates amplification.","A dynamic test only needs one pass of the truck at top speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"取樣率太低時峰值被削掉，算出的動力放大偏小；位移計架在會隨橋振動的臨時支架上，量到的其實是支架的運動；車輛位置沒有同步，事後就無法判斷峰值發生時車在哪裡。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Too low a sampling rate clips peaks and underestimates amplification; a displacement transducer on a temporary frame that vibrates with the bridge measures the frame; without synchronised vehicle position nobody can later tell where the truck was at the peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b058-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「試驗程序、封橋與安全管理」與「強迫振動與人群試驗」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Test procedure, closure and safety\" and \"Forced-vibration and crowd tests\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b058-v13-17","title":"試驗程序、封橋與安全管理：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Test procedure, closure and safety: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「試驗趟次矩陣」如何影響橋梁動態荷重試驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Test-run matrix” governs force, deformation or durability in “Dynamic bridge load testing”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"動態試驗通常依序進行：先量環境振動，再做慢速（TRB 入門所稱低於約 5 mph，即 8 km/h）的準靜態趟次，接著是不同車速的動態趟次，必要時在橋面放置木板做跳車試驗，最後再量一次環境振動確認橋梁狀態未改變。每一組條件重複三趟以上以評估離散度。試驗需要封閉交通，因此要預先排定趟次矩陣、時程與緊急開放程序，並在每一階段確認資料合理後才進入下一階段。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「試驗趟次矩陣」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A dynamic test usually runs in order: ambient vibration first, then quasi-static runs at crawl speed (below about 5 mph, or 8 km/h, as the TRB primer describes), then dynamic runs at several speeds, a plank or bump test where needed, and a final ambient record to confirm the bridge has not changed. Each condition is repeated three or more times to judge scatter. Testing requires a traffic closure, so the run matrix, schedule and emergency reopening procedure must be fixed in advance, with each stage's data checked for plausibility before moving on. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Test-run matrix” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：兩個車道 × 四種車速（20、40、60、80 km/h）× 三趟 = 24 趟，加上兩車道慢速各三趟共 30 趟；每趟含迴轉與歸零約 6 分鐘，需約 30×6 = 180 min = 3 小時封橋，另加前後環境振動量測。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Two lanes × four speeds (20, 40, 60 and 80 km/h) × three runs = 24 runs, plus three crawl runs in each lane, 30 runs in all; at about 6 minutes per run including turning and re-zeroing, the closure needs about 30×6 = 180 min = 3 hours, plus ambient records before and after.","failure":"常見誤解：「動態試驗只要讓卡車以最高速通過一次就夠了。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A dynamic test only needs one pass of the truck at top speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「試驗趟次矩陣」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Test-run matrix”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-17-k1","title":"試驗程序、封橋與安全管理","titleEn":"Test procedure, closure and safety","text":"動態試驗通常依序進行：先量環境振動，再做慢速（TRB 入門所稱低於約 5 mph，即 8 km/h）的準靜態趟次，接著是不同車速的動態趟次，必要時在橋面放置木板做跳車試驗，最後再量一次環境振動確認橋梁狀態未改變。每一組條件重複三趟以上以評估離散度。","textEn":"A dynamic test usually runs in order: ambient vibration first, then quasi-static runs at crawl speed (below about 5 mph, or 8 km/h, as the TRB primer describes), then dynamic runs at several speeds, a plank or bump test where needed, and a final ambient record to confirm the bridge has not changed. Each condition is repeated three or more times to judge scatter.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：動態試驗只要讓卡車以最高速通過一次就夠了。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A dynamic test only needs one pass of the truck at top speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「試驗程序、封橋與安全管理」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Test procedure, closure and safety\" is correct?","options":["動態試驗只要讓卡車以最高速通過一次就夠了。","人行橋只要強度設計通過，就不必做人群振動試驗。","動態試驗通常依序進行：先量環境振動，再做慢速（TRB 入門所稱低於約 5 mph，即 8 km/h）的準靜態趟次，接著是不同車速的動態趟次，必要時在橋面放置木板做跳車試驗，最後再量一次環境振動確認橋梁狀態未改變。"],"optionsEn":["A dynamic test only needs one pass of the truck at top speed.","If a footbridge passes its strength design, it needs no crowd vibration test.","A dynamic test usually runs in order: ambient vibration first, then quasi-static runs at crawl speed (below about 5 mph, or 8 km/h, as the TRB primer describes), then dynamic runs at several speeds, a plank or bump test where needed, and a final ambient record to confirm the bridge has not changed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"動態試驗通常依序進行：先量環境振動，再做慢速（TRB 入門所稱低於約 5 mph，即 8 km/h）的準靜態趟次，接著是不同車速的動態趟次，必要時在橋面放置木板做跳車試驗，最後再量一次環境振動確認橋梁狀態未改變。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A dynamic test usually runs in order: ambient vibration first, then quasi-static runs at crawl speed (below about 5 mph, or 8 km/h, as the TRB primer describes), then dynamic runs at several speeds, a plank or bump test where needed, and a final ambient record to confirm the bridge has not changed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b058-v13-18","title":"試驗程序、封橋與安全管理：定量估算","titleEn":"Test procedure, closure and safety: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「試驗趟次矩陣」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Test-run matrix” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：兩個車道 × 四種車速（20、40、60、80 km/h）× 三趟 = 24 趟，加上兩車道慢速各三趟共 30 趟；每趟含迴轉與歸零約 6 分鐘，需約 30×6 = 180 min = 3 小時封橋，另加前後環境振動量測。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Two lanes × four speeds (20, 40, 60 and 80 km/h) × three runs = 24 runs, plus three crawl runs in each lane, 30 runs in all; at about 6 minutes per run including turning and re-zeroing, the closure needs about 30×6 = 180 min = 3 hours, plus ambient records before and after. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：試驗主持人在每一趟後檢查關鍵通道峰值與預期值的比值，若超過停止準則（例如 1.2 倍）或出現未歸零的殘餘應變，即暫停並檢查橋梁與儀器；所有趟次以編號、時間、車速與車道記錄於試驗日誌。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After every run, the test director checks the ratio of peak to predicted value on key channels; if it exceeds the stop criterion, for example 1.2, or residual strain fails to return to zero, testing pauses for a bridge and instrument check.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"兩個車道 × 四種車速（20、40、60、80 km/h）× 三趟 = 24 趟，加上兩車道慢速各三趟共 30 趟；每趟含迴轉與歸零約 6 分鐘，需約 30×6 = 180 min = 3 小時封橋，另加前後環境振動量測。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Two lanes × four speeds (20, 40, 60 and 80 km/h) × three runs = 24 runs, plus three crawl runs in each lane, 30 runs in all; at about 6 minutes per run including turning and re-zeroing, the closure needs about 30×6 = 180 min = 3 hours, plus ambient records before and after. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「試驗程序、封橋與安全管理」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Test procedure, closure and safety\", which statement holds?","options":["兩個車道 × 四種車速（20、40、60、80 km/h）× 三趟 = 24 趟，加上兩車道慢速各三趟共 30 趟。","實測應變比計算低，就可以按比例直接提高橋梁的容許載重。","載重試驗通過一次，就證明橋梁永遠安全。"],"optionsEn":["Two lanes × four speeds (20, 40, 60 and 80 km/h) × three runs = 24 runs, plus three crawl runs in each lane, 30 runs in all.","If measured strain is lower than calculated, the permitted load can be raised in direct proportion.","Passing one load test proves the bridge safe forever."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩個車道 × 四種車速（20、40、60、80 km/h）× 三趟 = 24 趟，加上兩車道慢速各三趟共 30 趟；每趟含迴轉與歸零約 6 分鐘，需約 30×6 = 180 min = 3 小時封橋，另加前後環境振動量測。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Two lanes × four speeds (20, 40, 60 and 80 km/h) × three runs = 24 runs, plus three crawl runs in each lane, 30 runs in all; at about 6 minutes per run including turning and re-zeroing, the closure needs about 30×6 = 180 min = 3 hours, plus ambient records before and after. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b058-v13-19","title":"試驗程序、封橋與安全管理：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Test procedure, closure and safety: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「試驗趟次矩陣」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Test-run matrix” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"試驗主持人在每一趟後檢查關鍵通道峰值與預期值的比值，若超過停止準則（例如 1.2 倍）或出現未歸零的殘餘應變，即暫停並檢查橋梁與儀器；所有趟次以編號、時間、車速與車道記錄於試驗日誌。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After every run, the test director checks the ratio of peak to predicted value on key channels; if it exceeds the stop criterion, for example 1.2, or residual strain fails to return to zero, testing pauses for a bridge and instrument check. Every run is logged with number, time, speed and lane. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：高速趟次屬有風險的作業，須由交通主管機關核准封閉、設置緩衝區與救援車輛，試驗駕駛事先演練；本課只說明試驗設計邏輯，實際執行須依業主核准的試驗計畫與安全計畫辦理。","observationEn":"Site practice: High-speed runs are hazardous: the traffic authority must approve the closure, buffer zones and recovery vehicles must be in place and drivers must rehearse; this course explains test-design logic only, and real tests must follow the owner-approved test and safety plans.","failure":"注意干擾：為了縮短封橋時間而省略重複趟次，單一趟次受到風或駕駛偏移影響，得到的動力放大不具代表性；試驗車沒有按標線行駛或速度不穩，也會使不同趟次無法比較。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Skipping repeats to shorten the closure leaves single runs affected by wind or driver offset, so the measured amplification is unrepresentative; a truck that strays from its marked line or holds an unsteady speed makes runs incomparable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"試驗主持人在每一趟後檢查關鍵通道峰值與預期值的比值，若超過停止準則（例如 1.2 倍）或出現未歸零的殘餘應變，即暫停並檢查橋梁與儀器；所有趟次以編號、時間、車速與車道記錄於試驗日誌。","textEn":"After every run, the test director checks the ratio of peak to predicted value on key channels; if it exceeds the stop criterion, for example 1.2, or residual strain fails to return to zero, testing pauses for a bridge and instrument check. Every run is logged with number, time, speed and lane.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"高速趟次屬有風險的作業，須由交通主管機關核准封閉、設置緩衝區與救援車輛，試驗駕駛事先演練；本課只說明試驗設計邏輯，實際執行須依業主核准的試驗計畫與安全計畫辦理。","textEn":"High-speed runs are hazardous: the traffic authority must approve the closure, buffer zones and recovery vehicles must be in place and drivers must rehearse; this course explains test-design logic only, and real tests must follow the owner-approved test and safety plans.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「試驗程序、封橋與安全管理」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Test procedure, closure and safety\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","試驗主持人在每一趟後檢查關鍵通道峰值與預期值的比值，若超過停止準則（例如 1.2 倍）或出現未歸零的殘餘應變，即暫停並檢查橋梁與儀器。","只要垂直頻率避開 2 Hz，人行橋就不會有振動問題。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","After every run, the test director checks the ratio of peak to predicted value on key channels.","As long as the vertical frequency avoids 2 Hz, a footbridge will have no vibration problems."],"answer":1,"explanation":"試驗主持人在每一趟後檢查關鍵通道峰值與預期值的比值，若超過停止準則（例如 1.2 倍）或出現未歸零的殘餘應變，即暫停並檢查橋梁與儀器；所有趟次以編號、時間、車速與車道記錄於試驗日誌。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After every run, the test director checks the ratio of peak to predicted value on key channels; if it exceeds the stop criterion, for example 1.2, or residual strain fails to return to zero, testing pauses for a bridge and instrument check. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b058-v13-20","title":"試驗程序、封橋與安全管理：失效診斷","titleEn":"Test procedure, closure and safety: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「試驗趟次矩陣」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Test-run matrix” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為了縮短封橋時間而省略重複趟次，單一趟次受到風或駕駛偏移影響，得到的動力放大不具代表性；試驗車沒有按標線行駛或速度不穩，也會使不同趟次無法比較。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Skipping repeats to shorten the closure leaves single runs affected by wind or driver offset, so the measured amplification is unrepresentative; a truck that strays from its marked line or holds an unsteady speed makes runs incomparable. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：試驗需要封閉交通，因此要預先排定趟次矩陣、時程與緊急開放程序，並在每一階段確認資料合理後才進入下一階段。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Testing requires a traffic closure, so the run matrix, schedule and emergency reopening procedure must be fixed in advance, with each stage's data checked for plausibility before moving on.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「動態試驗只要讓卡車以最高速通過一次就夠了。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A dynamic test only needs one pass of the truck at top speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為了縮短封橋時間而省略重複趟次，單一趟次受到風或駕駛偏移影響，得到的動力放大不具代表性；試驗車沒有按標線行駛或速度不穩，也會使不同趟次無法比較。","textEn":"Skipping repeats to shorten the closure leaves single runs affected by wind or driver offset, so the measured amplification is unrepresentative; a truck that strays from its marked line or holds an unsteady speed makes runs incomparable.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「試驗程序、封橋與安全管理」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Test procedure, closure and safety\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","人行橋只要強度設計通過，就不必做人群振動試驗。","為了縮短封橋時間而省略重複趟次，單一趟次受到風或駕駛偏移影響，得到的動力放大不具代表性；試驗車沒有按標線行駛或速度不穩，也會使不同趟次無法比較。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","If a footbridge passes its strength design, it needs no crowd vibration test.","Skipping repeats to shorten the closure leaves single runs affected by wind or driver offset, so the measured amplification is unrepresentative."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為了縮短封橋時間而省略重複趟次，單一趟次受到風或駕駛偏移影響，得到的動力放大不具代表性；試驗車沒有按標線行駛或速度不穩，也會使不同趟次無法比較。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Skipping repeats to shorten the closure leaves single runs affected by wind or driver offset, so the measured amplification is unrepresentative; a truck that strays from its marked line or holds an unsteady speed makes runs incomparable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b058-v13-21","title":"強迫振動與人群試驗：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Forced-vibration and crowd tests: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「激振器與人群步行試驗」如何影響橋梁動態荷重試驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shaker and crowd walking tests” governs force, deformation or durability in “Dynamic bridge load testing”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"卡車通過只能短暫激起振動，要精確量測特定振態的頻率、振型與阻尼，常用偏心質量激振器在固定頻率持續激振，或以掃頻找出共振峰；人行橋則用可控制人數與步頻的人群試驗。千禧橋在 2000 年以最多 275 人在單一跨上進行人群試驗，找出側向振動隨人數突然增加的行為；改造完成後，Arup 再安排 2,000 人過橋驗證阻尼裝置的效果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「激振器與人群步行試驗」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A passing truck excites vibration only briefly, so measuring the frequency, shape and damping of a particular mode precisely calls for an eccentric-mass shaker driven steadily at one frequency or swept to find the resonant peak; footbridges use crowd tests with controlled numbers and pacing. In 2000 the Millennium Bridge was tested with crowds of up to 275 people on one span, revealing lateral vibration that jumped once numbers passed a threshold; after the retrofit, Arup had 2,000 people walk across to verify the damping devices. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Shaker and crowd walking tests” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：偏心質量激振力 F = m_e·e·ω²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Eccentric-mass shaker force F = m_e·e·ω².","failure":"常見誤解：「人行橋只要強度設計通過，就不必做人群振動試驗。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If a footbridge passes its strength design, it needs no crowd vibration test.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「激振器與人群步行試驗」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Shaker and crowd walking tests”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-21-k1","title":"強迫振動與人群試驗","titleEn":"Forced-vibration and crowd tests","text":"卡車通過只能短暫激起振動，要精確量測特定振態的頻率、振型與阻尼，常用偏心質量激振器在固定頻率持續激振，或以掃頻找出共振峰；人行橋則用可控制人數與步頻的人群試驗。千禧橋在 2000 年以最多 275 人在單一跨上進行人群試驗，找出側向振動隨人數突然增加的行為；改造完成後，Arup 再安排 2,000 人過橋驗證阻尼裝置的效果。","textEn":"A passing truck excites vibration only briefly, so measuring the frequency, shape and damping of a particular mode precisely calls for an eccentric-mass shaker driven steadily at one frequency or swept to find the resonant peak; footbridges use crowd tests with controlled numbers and pacing. In 2000 the Millennium Bridge was tested with crowds of up to 275 people on one span, revealing lateral vibration that jumped once numbers passed a threshold; after the retrofit, Arup had 2,000 people walk across to verify the damping devices.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：人行橋只要強度設計通過，就不必做人群振動試驗。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If a footbridge passes its strength design, it needs no crowd vibration test. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「強迫振動與人群試驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Forced-vibration and crowd tests\" is correct?","options":["卡車通過只能短暫激起振動，要精確量測特定振態的頻率、振型與阻尼，常用偏心質量激振器在固定頻率持續激振，或以掃頻找出共振峰；人行橋則用可控制人數與步頻的人群試驗。","人行橋只要強度設計通過，就不必做人群振動試驗。","實測頻率比模型高，就代表橋梁沒有任何問題。"],"optionsEn":["A passing truck excites vibration only briefly, so measuring the frequency, shape and damping of a particular mode precisely calls for an eccentric-mass shaker driven steadily at one frequency or swept to find the resonant peak.","If a footbridge passes its strength design, it needs no crowd vibration test.","A measured frequency higher than the model means the bridge has no problems."],"answer":0,"explanation":"卡車通過只能短暫激起振動，要精確量測特定振態的頻率、振型與阻尼，常用偏心質量激振器在固定頻率持續激振，或以掃頻找出共振峰；人行橋則用可控制人數與步頻的人群試驗。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A passing truck excites vibration only briefly, so measuring the frequency, shape and damping of a particular mode precisely calls for an eccentric-mass shaker driven steadily at one frequency or swept to find the resonant peak; footbridges use crowd tests with controlled numbers and pacing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b058-v13-22","title":"強迫振動與人群試驗：定量估算","titleEn":"Forced-vibration and crowd tests: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「激振器與人群步行試驗」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shaker and crowd walking tests” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：偏心質量激振力 F = m_e·e·ω²。m_e·e = 2 kg·m、f = 2 Hz（ω = 12.57 rad/s）：F = 2×157.9 ≈ 316 N。模態質量 M = 50,000 kg、模態勁度 k = M·ω² ≈ 7.9×10⁶ N/m、ζ = 1%：共振振幅 x = F/(2ζk) ≈ 2.0 mm，加速度 ω²x ≈ 0.32 m/s²。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Eccentric-mass shaker force F = m_e·e·ω². With m_e·e = 2 kg·m and f = 2 Hz (ω = 12.57 rad/s), F = 2×157.9 ≈ 316 N. For modal mass M = 50,000 kg, modal stiffness k = M·ω² ≈ 7.9×10⁶ N/m and ζ = 1%, the resonant amplitude is x = F/(2ζk) ≈ 2.0 mm and the acceleration ω²x ≈ 0.32 m/s². Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：掃頻時以小步距逐步改變頻率，每一頻率等待穩態後記錄力與加速度，繪出頻率響應函數求共振頻率與阻尼；人群試驗以影像或計數器記錄人數與分布，並設定即時顯示的加速度中止門檻。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: In a sweep, step the frequency in small increments, wait for steady state at each and record force and acceleration, then build the frequency response function to obtain resonance and damping; in crowd tests, record numbers and distribution with video or counters and set a live-displayed acceleration stop threshold.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"偏心質量激振力 F = m_e·e·ω²。m_e·e = 2 kg·m、f = 2 Hz（ω = 12.57 rad/s）：F = 2×157.9 ≈ 316 N。模態質量 M = 50,000 kg、模態勁度 k = M·ω² ≈ 7.9×10⁶ N/m、ζ = 1%：共振振幅 x = F/(2ζk) ≈ 2.0 mm，加速度 ω²x ≈ 0.32 m/s²。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Eccentric-mass shaker force F = m_e·e·ω². With m_e·e = 2 kg·m and f = 2 Hz (ω = 12.57 rad/s), F = 2×157.9 ≈ 316 N. For modal mass M = 50,000 kg, modal stiffness k = M·ω² ≈ 7.9×10⁶ N/m and ζ = 1%, the resonant amplitude is x = F/(2ζk) ≈ 2.0 mm and the acceleration ω²x ≈ 0.32 m/s². Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「強迫振動與人群試驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Forced-vibration and crowd tests\", which statement holds?","options":["加大構件斷面一定是解決人行橋振動最有效的方法。","偏心質量激振力 F = m_e·e·ω²。","車速越快，橋梁的動力放大一定越大。"],"optionsEn":["Enlarging member sections is always the most effective cure for footbridge vibration.","Eccentric-mass shaker force F = m_e·e·ω².","The faster the vehicle, the larger the dynamic amplification must be."],"answer":1,"explanation":"偏心質量激振力 F = m_e·e·ω²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Eccentric-mass shaker force F = m_e·e·ω². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b058-v13-23","title":"強迫振動與人群試驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Forced-vibration and crowd tests: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「激振器與人群步行試驗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shaker and crowd walking tests” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"掃頻時以小步距逐步改變頻率，每一頻率等待穩態後記錄力與加速度，繪出頻率響應函數求共振頻率與阻尼；人群試驗以影像或計數器記錄人數與分布，並設定即時顯示的加速度中止門檻。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"In a sweep, step the frequency in small increments, wait for steady state at each and record force and acceleration, then build the frequency response function to obtain resonance and damping; in crowd tests, record numbers and distribution with video or counters and set a live-displayed acceleration stop threshold. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：人群試驗須先完成風險評估：人數分級逐步增加、出入口管制、醫護與廣播、加速度即時顯示與中止權責；參與者事前須了解試驗內容，所有分級與中止決定由試驗主持工程師記錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: A crowd test needs a prior risk assessment: stepwise crowd stages, controlled entry and exit, first aid and public address, live acceleration display and a clear stop authority; participants are briefed in advance, and the test director records every stage and stop decision.","failure":"注意干擾：激振器若固定在不夠剛的位置，量到的是局部板件振動而非整體振態；人群試驗若沒有中止門檻，側向同步一旦觸發，人群可能在擺動中失去平衡或擠向欄杆。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A shaker fixed at a flexible spot measures local plate vibration rather than the global mode; a crowd test without a stop threshold can see people lose balance or crowd the railings once lateral lock-in starts. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"掃頻時以小步距逐步改變頻率，每一頻率等待穩態後記錄力與加速度，繪出頻率響應函數求共振頻率與阻尼；人群試驗以影像或計數器記錄人數與分布，並設定即時顯示的加速度中止門檻。","textEn":"In a sweep, step the frequency in small increments, wait for steady state at each and record force and acceleration, then build the frequency response function to obtain resonance and damping; in crowd tests, record numbers and distribution with video or counters and set a live-displayed acceleration stop threshold.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"人群試驗須先完成風險評估：人數分級逐步增加、出入口管制、醫護與廣播、加速度即時顯示與中止權責；參與者事前須了解試驗內容，所有分級與中止決定由試驗主持工程師記錄。","textEn":"A crowd test needs a prior risk assessment: stepwise crowd stages, controlled entry and exit, first aid and public address, live acceleration display and a clear stop authority; participants are briefed in advance, and the test director records every stage and stop decision.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「強迫振動與人群試驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Forced-vibration and crowd tests\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","載重試驗用的車越重，得到的結論就越可靠。","掃頻時以小步距逐步改變頻率，每一頻率等待穩態後記錄力與加速度，繪出頻率響應函數求共振頻率與阻尼。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The heavier the test vehicle, the more reliable the conclusions.","In a sweep, step the frequency in small increments, wait for steady state at each and record force and acceleration, then build the frequency response function to obtain resonance and damping."],"answer":2,"explanation":"掃頻時以小步距逐步改變頻率，每一頻率等待穩態後記錄力與加速度，繪出頻率響應函數求共振頻率與阻尼；人群試驗以影像或計數器記錄人數與分布，並設定即時顯示的加速度中止門檻。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"In a sweep, step the frequency in small increments, wait for steady state at each and record force and acceleration, then build the frequency response function to obtain resonance and damping; in crowd tests, record numbers and distribution with video or counters and set a live-displayed acceleration stop threshold. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b058-v13-24","title":"強迫振動與人群試驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Forced-vibration and crowd tests: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「激振器與人群步行試驗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shaker and crowd walking tests” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"激振器若固定在不夠剛的位置，量到的是局部板件振動而非整體振態；人群試驗若沒有中止門檻，側向同步一旦觸發，人群可能在擺動中失去平衡或擠向欄杆。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A shaker fixed at a flexible spot measures local plate vibration rather than the global mode; a crowd test without a stop threshold can see people lose balance or crowd the railings once lateral lock-in starts. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：千禧橋在 2000 年以最多 275 人在單一跨上進行人群試驗，找出側向振動隨人數突然增加的行為；改造完成後，Arup 再安排 2,000 人過橋驗證阻尼裝置的效果。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: In 2000 the Millennium Bridge was tested with crowds of up to 275 people on one span, revealing lateral vibration that jumped once numbers passed a threshold; after the retrofit, Arup had 2,000 people walk across to verify the damping devices.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「人行橋只要強度設計通過，就不必做人群振動試驗。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If a footbridge passes its strength design, it needs no crowd vibration test.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"激振器若固定在不夠剛的位置，量到的是局部板件振動而非整體振態；人群試驗若沒有中止門檻，側向同步一旦觸發，人群可能在擺動中失去平衡或擠向欄杆。","textEn":"A shaker fixed at a flexible spot measures local plate vibration rather than the global mode; a crowd test without a stop threshold can see people lose balance or crowd the railings once lateral lock-in starts.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「強迫振動與人群試驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Forced-vibration and crowd tests\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["激振器若固定在不夠剛的位置，量到的是局部板件振動而非整體振態；人群試驗若沒有中止門檻，側向同步一旦觸發，人群可能在擺動中失去平衡或擠向欄杆。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","實測頻率比模型高，就代表橋梁沒有任何問題。"],"optionsEn":["A shaker fixed at a flexible spot measures local plate vibration rather than the global mode.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A measured frequency higher than the model means the bridge has no problems."],"answer":0,"explanation":"激振器若固定在不夠剛的位置，量到的是局部板件振動而非整體振態；人群試驗若沒有中止門檻，側向同步一旦觸發，人群可能在擺動中失去平衡或擠向欄杆。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A shaker fixed at a flexible spot measures local plate vibration rather than the global mode; a crowd test without a stop threshold can see people lose balance or crowd the railings once lateral lock-in starts. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b058-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「動力放大、頻率與勁度判讀」與「模型修正與載重評等」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Interpreting amplification, frequency and stiffness\" and \"Model updating and load rating\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b058-v13-25","title":"動力放大、頻率與勁度判讀：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Interpreting amplification, frequency and stiffness: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「動態與準靜態歷時」如何影響橋梁動態荷重試驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dynamic and quasi-static histories” governs force, deformation or durability in “Dynamic bridge load testing”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"一趟高速通過的應變歷時包含兩部分：隨車輛位置緩慢變化的準靜態成分，以及橋梁自身振動造成的動態成分。可用低通濾波從高速趟次中分離準靜態成分，或直接與慢速趟次比較，求得動力放大。車輛離橋後的自由振動可用頻譜分析得到自振頻率，與模型比較即可判斷實際勁度：頻率與勁度的平方根成正比，所以頻率高約 6% 代表勁度高約 13%。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「動態與準靜態歷時」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A strain history from a fast run contains two parts: a quasi-static component that follows vehicle position slowly, and a dynamic component from the bridge's own vibration. Low-pass filtering separates the quasi-static part from a fast run, or the fast run can be compared directly with a crawl run, to obtain amplification. The free vibration after the truck leaves gives natural frequencies by spectral analysis, and comparing them with the model reveals actual stiffness: frequency varies with the square root of stiffness, so a frequency about 6% higher means a stiffness about 13% higher. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Dynamic and quasi-static histories” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：慢速峰值 120 με、80 km/h 峰值 142 με：DAF = 142/120 ≈ 1.18。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Crawl peak 120 με and 80 km/h peak 142 με give DAF = 142/120 ≈ 1.18.","failure":"常見誤解：「實測頻率比模型高，就代表橋梁沒有任何問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A measured frequency higher than the model means the bridge has no problems.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「動態與準靜態歷時」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Dynamic and quasi-static histories”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-25-k1","title":"動力放大、頻率與勁度判讀","titleEn":"Interpreting amplification, frequency and stiffness","text":"一趟高速通過的應變歷時包含兩部分：隨車輛位置緩慢變化的準靜態成分，以及橋梁自身振動造成的動態成分。可用低通濾波從高速趟次中分離準靜態成分，或直接與慢速趟次比較，求得動力放大。","textEn":"A strain history from a fast run contains two parts: a quasi-static component that follows vehicle position slowly, and a dynamic component from the bridge's own vibration. Low-pass filtering separates the quasi-static part from a fast run, or the fast run can be compared directly with a crawl run, to obtain amplification.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：實測頻率比模型高，就代表橋梁沒有任何問題。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A measured frequency higher than the model means the bridge has no problems. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「動力放大、頻率與勁度判讀」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Interpreting amplification, frequency and stiffness\" is correct?","options":["實測頻率比模型高，就代表橋梁沒有任何問題。","一趟高速通過的應變歷時包含兩部分：隨車輛位置緩慢變化的準靜態成分，以及橋梁自身振動造成的動態成分。","實測應變比計算低，就可以按比例直接提高橋梁的容許載重。"],"optionsEn":["A measured frequency higher than the model means the bridge has no problems.","A strain history from a fast run contains two parts: a quasi-static component that follows vehicle position slowly, and a dynamic component from the bridge's own vibration.","If measured strain is lower than calculated, the permitted load can be raised in direct proportion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一趟高速通過的應變歷時包含兩部分：隨車輛位置緩慢變化的準靜態成分，以及橋梁自身振動造成的動態成分。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A strain history from a fast run contains two parts: a quasi-static component that follows vehicle position slowly, and a dynamic component from the bridge's own vibration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b058-v13-26","title":"動力放大、頻率與勁度判讀：定量估算","titleEn":"Interpreting amplification, frequency and stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「動態與準靜態歷時」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dynamic and quasi-static histories” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：慢速峰值 120 με、80 km/h 峰值 142 με：DAF = 142/120 ≈ 1.18。第一彎曲頻率 f = (π/2L²)·√(EI/m)，L = 30 m、EI = 8.0×10¹⁰ N·m²、m = 12,000 kg/m：f_m ≈ 4.51 Hz；實測 4.80 Hz，勁度比 (4.80/4.51)² ≈ 1.13，實際勁度約高 13%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Crawl peak 120 με and 80 km/h peak 142 με give DAF = 142/120 ≈ 1.18. The first bending frequency is f = (π/2L²)·√(EI/m); with L = 30 m, EI = 8.0×10¹⁰ N·m² and m = 12,000 kg/m, f_m ≈ 4.51 Hz. A measured 4.80 Hz gives a stiffness ratio (4.80/4.51)² ≈ 1.13, about 13% stiffer than modelled. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以至少兩種方式（慢速比較與濾波分離）計算動力放大，結果應一致；頻率以多趟自由振動與環境振動資料交叉確認，並記錄試驗時溫度，以判斷差異是否來自護欄、鋪面參與或支承束制。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compute amplification by at least two routes, crawl comparison and filtering, and require agreement; confirm frequencies with several free-vibration records and ambient data, and record test temperature to judge whether differences come from barriers, surfacing or bearing restraint.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"慢速峰值 120 με、80 km/h 峰值 142 με：DAF = 142/120 ≈ 1.18。第一彎曲頻率 f = (π/2L²)·√(EI/m)，L = 30 m、EI = 8.0×10¹⁰ N·m²、m = 12,000 kg/m：f_m ≈ 4.51 Hz；實測 4.80 Hz，勁度比 (4.80/4.51)² ≈ 1.13，實際勁度約高 13%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Crawl peak 120 με and 80 km/h peak 142 με give DAF = 142/120 ≈ 1.18. The first bending frequency is f = (π/2L²)·√(EI/m); with L = 30 m, EI = 8.0×10¹⁰ N·m² and m = 12,000 kg/m, f_m ≈ 4.51 Hz. A measured 4.80 Hz gives a stiffness ratio (4.80/4.51)² ≈ 1.13, about 13% stiffer than modelled. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「動力放大、頻率與勁度判讀」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Interpreting amplification, frequency and stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["載重試驗通過一次，就證明橋梁永遠安全。","只要垂直頻率避開 2 Hz，人行橋就不會有振動問題。","慢速峰值 120 με、80 km/h 峰值 142 με：DAF = 142/120 ≈ 1.18。"],"optionsEn":["Passing one load test proves the bridge safe forever.","As long as the vertical frequency avoids 2 Hz, a footbridge will have no vibration problems.","Crawl peak 120 με and 80 km/h peak 142 με give DAF = 142/120 ≈ 1.18."],"answer":2,"explanation":"慢速峰值 120 με、80 km/h 峰值 142 με：DAF = 142/120 ≈ 1.18。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Crawl peak 120 με and 80 km/h peak 142 με give DAF = 142/120 ≈ 1.18. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b058-v13-27","title":"動力放大、頻率與勁度判讀：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Interpreting amplification, frequency and stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「動態與準靜態歷時」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dynamic and quasi-static histories” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以至少兩種方式（慢速比較與濾波分離）計算動力放大，結果應一致；頻率以多趟自由振動與環境振動資料交叉確認，並記錄試驗時溫度，以判斷差異是否來自護欄、鋪面參與或支承束制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compute amplification by at least two routes, crawl comparison and filtering, and require agreement; confirm frequencies with several free-vibration records and ambient data, and record test temperature to judge whether differences come from barriers, surfacing or bearing restraint. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：判讀報告要附上每一趟的原始歷時圖、濾波參數與頻譜圖，並說明實測與模型差異的可能來源（非結構構件、支承、溫度）；差異超過預定範圍時必須有工程解釋，不能直接調整模型參數使其吻合。","observationEn":"Site practice: The interpretation report should attach each run's raw history, filter settings and spectrum, and explain likely sources of difference between test and model (non-structural elements, bearings, temperature); any difference beyond a preset range needs an engineering explanation, not a quiet parameter tweak to force agreement.","failure":"注意干擾：低通濾波截止頻率選得太低，會把部分準靜態峰值也濾掉，使動力放大被高估；把較高的實測頻率直接解讀為橋梁很健康，卻沒發現那是支承卡死造成的額外束制，反而掩蓋了另一種問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A low-pass cut-off set too low also removes part of the quasi-static peak and overstates amplification; reading a higher measured frequency simply as a healthy bridge can miss that it comes from seized bearings, masking a different problem. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以至少兩種方式（慢速比較與濾波分離）計算動力放大，結果應一致；頻率以多趟自由振動與環境振動資料交叉確認，並記錄試驗時溫度，以判斷差異是否來自護欄、鋪面參與或支承束制。","textEn":"Compute amplification by at least two routes, crawl comparison and filtering, and require agreement; confirm frequencies with several free-vibration records and ambient data, and record test temperature to judge whether differences come from barriers, surfacing or bearing restraint.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"判讀報告要附上每一趟的原始歷時圖、濾波參數與頻譜圖，並說明實測與模型差異的可能來源（非結構構件、支承、溫度）；差異超過預定範圍時必須有工程解釋，不能直接調整模型參數使其吻合。","textEn":"The interpretation report should attach each run's raw history, filter settings and spectrum, and explain likely sources of difference between test and model (non-structural elements, bearings, temperature); any difference beyond a preset range needs an engineering explanation, not a quiet parameter tweak to force agreement.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「動力放大、頻率與勁度判讀」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Interpreting amplification, frequency and stiffness\"?","options":["以至少兩種方式（慢速比較與濾波分離）計算動力放大，結果應一致。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要量到最大應變，取樣率高低並不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Compute amplification by at least two routes, crawl comparison and filtering, and require agreement.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","As long as the maximum strain is captured, sampling rate does not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以至少兩種方式（慢速比較與濾波分離）計算動力放大，結果應一致；頻率以多趟自由振動與環境振動資料交叉確認，並記錄試驗時溫度，以判斷差異是否來自護欄、鋪面參與或支承束制。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compute amplification by at least two routes, crawl comparison and filtering, and require agreement; confirm frequencies with several free-vibration records and ambient data, and record test temperature to judge whether differences come from barriers, surfacing or bearing restraint. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b058-v13-28","title":"動力放大、頻率與勁度判讀：失效診斷","titleEn":"Interpreting amplification, frequency and stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「動態與準靜態歷時」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dynamic and quasi-static histories” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"低通濾波截止頻率選得太低，會把部分準靜態峰值也濾掉，使動力放大被高估；把較高的實測頻率直接解讀為橋梁很健康，卻沒發現那是支承卡死造成的額外束制，反而掩蓋了另一種問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A low-pass cut-off set too low also removes part of the quasi-static peak and overstates amplification; reading a higher measured frequency simply as a healthy bridge can miss that it comes from seized bearings, masking a different problem. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：車輛離橋後的自由振動可用頻譜分析得到自振頻率，與模型比較即可判斷實際勁度：頻率與勁度的平方根成正比，所以頻率高約 6% 代表勁度高約 13%。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The free vibration after the truck leaves gives natural frequencies by spectral analysis, and comparing them with the model reveals actual stiffness: frequency varies with the square root of stiffness, so a frequency about 6% higher means a stiffness about 13% higher.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「實測頻率比模型高，就代表橋梁沒有任何問題。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A measured frequency higher than the model means the bridge has no problems.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"低通濾波截止頻率選得太低，會把部分準靜態峰值也濾掉，使動力放大被高估；把較高的實測頻率直接解讀為橋梁很健康，卻沒發現那是支承卡死造成的額外束制，反而掩蓋了另一種問題。","textEn":"A low-pass cut-off set too low also removes part of the quasi-static peak and overstates amplification; reading a higher measured frequency simply as a healthy bridge can miss that it comes from seized bearings, masking a different problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「動力放大、頻率與勁度判讀」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Interpreting amplification, frequency and stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","低通濾波截止頻率選得太低，會把部分準靜態峰值也濾掉，使動力放大被高估。","實測應變比計算低，就可以按比例直接提高橋梁的容許載重。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A low-pass cut-off set too low also removes part of the quasi-static peak and overstates amplification.","If measured strain is lower than calculated, the permitted load can be raised in direct proportion."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低通濾波截止頻率選得太低，會把部分準靜態峰值也濾掉，使動力放大被高估；把較高的實測頻率直接解讀為橋梁很健康，卻沒發現那是支承卡死造成的額外束制，反而掩蓋了另一種問題。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A low-pass cut-off set too low also removes part of the quasi-static peak and overstates amplification; reading a higher measured frequency simply as a healthy bridge can miss that it comes from seized bearings, masking a different problem. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b058-v13-29","title":"模型修正與載重評等：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Model updating and load rating: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「試驗修正係數」如何影響橋梁動態荷重試驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Test adjustment factor” governs force, deformation or durability in “Dynamic bridge load testing”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"試驗的最終用途常是載重評等：若實測應變低於計算值，表示橋梁有計算未考慮的有利機制，例如未設計為組合作用的混凝土橋面、護欄參與、支承束制或較佳的橫向分配。AASHTO 橋梁評估手冊允許以試驗修正係數調整計算評等，但必須判斷這些有利機制在更重載重下是否仍然可靠；支承束制或未設計的組合作用可能在重載下失效，因此修正量要打折。動態試驗得到的實測動力放大也可取代規範值，前提是路面條件被納入管理。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「試驗修正係數」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The usual end use of a test is load rating: measured strains below calculation show favourable mechanisms the calculation ignored, such as unintended composite action with the deck, barrier participation, bearing restraint or better lateral distribution. The AASHTO Manual for Bridge Evaluation lets a test adjustment factor modify the calculated rating, but engineers must judge whether those mechanisms remain reliable under heavier loads; bearing restraint or unintended composite action can break down under heavy load, so the benefit is discounted. A measured dynamic amplification can also replace the code value, provided the surface condition is managed. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Test adjustment factor” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：評等修正 RF_T = RF_c·K，K = 1 + K_a·K_b。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Rating adjustment RF_T = RF_c·K with K = 1 + K_a·K_b.","failure":"常見誤解：「實測應變比計算低，就可以按比例直接提高橋梁的容許載重。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If measured strain is lower than calculated, the permitted load can be raised in direct proportion.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「試驗修正係數」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Test adjustment factor”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-29-k1","title":"模型修正與載重評等","titleEn":"Model updating and load rating","text":"試驗的最終用途常是載重評等：若實測應變低於計算值，表示橋梁有計算未考慮的有利機制，例如未設計為組合作用的混凝土橋面、護欄參與、支承束制或較佳的橫向分配。AASHTO 橋梁評估手冊允許以試驗修正係數調整計算評等，但必須判斷這些有利機制在更重載重下是否仍然可靠；支承束制或未設計的組合作用可能在重載下失效，因此修正量要打折。","textEn":"The usual end use of a test is load rating: measured strains below calculation show favourable mechanisms the calculation ignored, such as unintended composite action with the deck, barrier participation, bearing restraint or better lateral distribution. The AASHTO Manual for Bridge Evaluation lets a test adjustment factor modify the calculated rating, but engineers must judge whether those mechanisms remain reliable under heavier loads; bearing restraint or unintended composite action can break down under heavy load, so the benefit is discounted.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：實測應變比計算低，就可以按比例直接提高橋梁的容許載重。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If measured strain is lower than calculated, the permitted load can be raised in direct proportion. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模型修正與載重評等」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Model updating and load rating\" is correct?","options":["實測應變比計算低，就可以按比例直接提高橋梁的容許載重。","加大構件斷面一定是解決人行橋振動最有效的方法。","試驗的最終用途常是載重評等：若實測應變低於計算值，表示橋梁有計算未考慮的有利機制，例如未設計為組合作用的混凝土橋面、護欄參與、支承束制或較佳的橫向分配。"],"optionsEn":["If measured strain is lower than calculated, the permitted load can be raised in direct proportion.","Enlarging member sections is always the most effective cure for footbridge vibration.","The usual end use of a test is load rating: measured strains below calculation show favourable mechanisms the calculation ignored, such as unintended composite action with the deck, barrier participation, bearing restraint or better lateral distribution."],"answer":2,"explanation":"試驗的最終用途常是載重評等：若實測應變低於計算值，表示橋梁有計算未考慮的有利機制，例如未設計為組合作用的混凝土橋面、護欄參與、支承束制或較佳的橫向分配。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The usual end use of a test is load rating: measured strains below calculation show favourable mechanisms the calculation ignored, such as unintended composite action with the deck, barrier participation, bearing restraint or better lateral distribution. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b058-v13-30","title":"模型修正與載重評等：定量估算","titleEn":"Model updating and load rating: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「試驗修正係數」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Test adjustment factor” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：評等修正 RF_T = RF_c·K，K = 1 + K_a·K_b。計算應變 ε_c = 150 με、實測 ε_T = 120 με：K_a = ε_c/ε_T − 1 = 0.25；取 K_b = 0.5（試驗載重相對評等載重較低、有利機制不完全可靠），K = 1.125。原評等 RF_c = 0.92 提升為 0.92×1.125 ≈ 1.04。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Rating adjustment RF_T = RF_c·K with K = 1 + K_a·K_b. With calculated strain ε_c = 150 με and measured ε_T = 120 με, K_a = ε_c/ε_T − 1 = 0.25; taking K_b = 0.5 (test load low relative to the rating load, favourable mechanisms not fully reliable) gives K = 1.125, raising RF_c = 0.92 to 0.92×1.125 ≈ 1.04. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以實測資料更新有限元素模型的邊界勁度與組合作用程度，檢查模型能否同時重現多個量測點與多個車道的反應，而不只是單一點；修正係數的取值依據要逐項說明，並由評等工程師簽認。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Update boundary stiffness and degree of composite action in the finite-element model from the test data, and check that it reproduces responses at many gauges and in several lanes, not just one point; justify each term of the adjustment factor and have the rating engineer sign it.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"評等修正 RF_T = RF_c·K，K = 1 + K_a·K_b。計算應變 ε_c = 150 με、實測 ε_T = 120 με：K_a = ε_c/ε_T − 1 = 0.25；取 K_b = 0.5（試驗載重相對評等載重較低、有利機制不完全可靠），K = 1.125。原評等 RF_c = 0.92 提升為 0.92×1.125 ≈ 1.04。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Rating adjustment RF_T = RF_c·K with K = 1 + K_a·K_b. With calculated strain ε_c = 150 με and measured ε_T = 120 με, K_a = ε_c/ε_T − 1 = 0.25; taking K_b = 0.5 (test load low relative to the rating load, favourable mechanisms not fully reliable) gives K = 1.125, raising RF_c = 0.92 to 0.92×1.125 ≈ 1.04. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模型修正與載重評等」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Model updating and load rating\", which statement holds?","options":["評等修正 RF_T = RF_c·K，K = 1 + K_a·K_b。","車速越快，橋梁的動力放大一定越大。","載重試驗用的車越重，得到的結論就越可靠。"],"optionsEn":["Rating adjustment RF_T = RF_c·K with K = 1 + K_a·K_b.","The faster the vehicle, the larger the dynamic amplification must be.","The heavier the test vehicle, the more reliable the conclusions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"評等修正 RF_T = RF_c·K，K = 1 + K_a·K_b。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Rating adjustment RF_T = RF_c·K with K = 1 + K_a·K_b. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b058-v13-31","title":"模型修正與載重評等：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Model updating and load rating: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「試驗修正係數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Test adjustment factor” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以實測資料更新有限元素模型的邊界勁度與組合作用程度，檢查模型能否同時重現多個量測點與多個車道的反應，而不只是單一點；修正係數的取值依據要逐項說明，並由評等工程師簽認。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Update boundary stiffness and degree of composite action in the finite-element model from the test data, and check that it reproduces responses at many gauges and in several lanes, not just one point; justify each term of the adjustment factor and have the rating engineer sign it. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：以試驗提高評等時，報告必須列出所依賴的有利機制、可能失效的條件與重新試驗的觸發事件（例如支承更換、橋面重鋪、超重車輛增加），並明訂評等結果的適用期限。","observationEn":"Site practice: When a test raises a rating, the report must list the favourable mechanisms relied on, the conditions under which they could fail and the events that trigger retesting (bearing replacement, resurfacing, more overweight traffic), and state how long the rating remains valid.","failure":"注意干擾：把支承卡死造成的有利束制當成永久性能而大幅提高評等，若支承日後鬆動或更換，實際應力會回到計算值以上；只用單一量測點修正模型，可能把局部效應誤當成整體行為。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating restraint from seized bearings as permanent and raising the rating sharply leaves stresses above calculation once the bearings free up or are replaced; updating the model on a single gauge can mistake a local effect for global behaviour. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以實測資料更新有限元素模型的邊界勁度與組合作用程度，檢查模型能否同時重現多個量測點與多個車道的反應，而不只是單一點；修正係數的取值依據要逐項說明，並由評等工程師簽認。","textEn":"Update boundary stiffness and degree of composite action in the finite-element model from the test data, and check that it reproduces responses at many gauges and in several lanes, not just one point; justify each term of the adjustment factor and have the rating engineer sign it.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"以試驗提高評等時，報告必須列出所依賴的有利機制、可能失效的條件與重新試驗的觸發事件（例如支承更換、橋面重鋪、超重車輛增加），並明訂評等結果的適用期限。","textEn":"When a test raises a rating, the report must list the favourable mechanisms relied on, the conditions under which they could fail and the events that trigger retesting (bearing replacement, resurfacing, more overweight traffic), and state how long the rating remains valid.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模型修正與載重評等」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Model updating and load rating\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以實測資料更新有限元素模型的邊界勁度與組合作用程度，檢查模型能否同時重現多個量測點與多個車道的反應，而不只是單一點。","動態試驗只要讓卡車以最高速通過一次就夠了。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Update boundary stiffness and degree of composite action in the finite-element model from the test data, and check that it reproduces responses at many gauges and in several lanes, not just one point.","A dynamic test only needs one pass of the truck at top speed."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以實測資料更新有限元素模型的邊界勁度與組合作用程度，檢查模型能否同時重現多個量測點與多個車道的反應，而不只是單一點；修正係數的取值依據要逐項說明，並由評等工程師簽認。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Update boundary stiffness and degree of composite action in the finite-element model from the test data, and check that it reproduces responses at many gauges and in several lanes, not just one point; justify each term of the adjustment factor and have the rating engineer sign it. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b058-v13-32","title":"模型修正與載重評等：失效診斷","titleEn":"Model updating and load rating: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「試驗修正係數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Test adjustment factor” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把支承卡死造成的有利束制當成永久性能而大幅提高評等，若支承日後鬆動或更換，實際應力會回到計算值以上；只用單一量測點修正模型，可能把局部效應誤當成整體行為。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating restraint from seized bearings as permanent and raising the rating sharply leaves stresses above calculation once the bearings free up or are replaced; updating the model on a single gauge can mistake a local effect for global behaviour. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：動態試驗得到的實測動力放大也可取代規範值，前提是路面條件被納入管理。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A measured dynamic amplification can also replace the code value, provided the surface condition is managed.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「實測應變比計算低，就可以按比例直接提高橋梁的容許載重。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If measured strain is lower than calculated, the permitted load can be raised in direct proportion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把支承卡死造成的有利束制當成永久性能而大幅提高評等，若支承日後鬆動或更換，實際應力會回到計算值以上；只用單一量測點修正模型，可能把局部效應誤當成整體行為。","textEn":"Treating restraint from seized bearings as permanent and raising the rating sharply leaves stresses above calculation once the bearings free up or are replaced; updating the model on a single gauge can mistake a local effect for global behaviour.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模型修正與載重評等」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Model updating and load rating\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","加大構件斷面一定是解決人行橋振動最有效的方法。","把支承卡死造成的有利束制當成永久性能而大幅提高評等，若支承日後鬆動或更換，實際應力會回到計算值以上；只用單一量測點修正模型，可能把局部效應誤當成整體行為。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Enlarging member sections is always the most effective cure for footbridge vibration.","Treating restraint from seized bearings as permanent and raising the rating sharply leaves stresses above calculation once the bearings free up or are replaced."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把支承卡死造成的有利束制當成永久性能而大幅提高評等，若支承日後鬆動或更換，實際應力會回到計算值以上；只用單一量測點修正模型，可能把局部效應誤當成整體行為。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating restraint from seized bearings as permanent and raising the rating sharply leaves stresses above calculation once the bearings free up or are replaced; updating the model on a single gauge can mistake a local effect for global behaviour. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b058-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「舒適度準則與振動改善」與「試驗報告、重現性與基準交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Comfort criteria and vibration retrofit\" and \"Test report, repeatability and baseline handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b058-v13-33","title":"舒適度準則與振動改善：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Comfort criteria and vibration retrofit: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「黏滯阻尼器與調諧質量阻尼器」如何影響橋梁動態荷重試驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Viscous dampers and TMDs” governs force, deformation or durability in “Dynamic bridge load testing”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"人行橋與輕量橋梁的振動多半是使用性問題而非強度問題，判斷標準是加速度：歐洲規範 EN 1990 附錄 A2 建議人行橋垂直加速度不超過 0.7 m/s²，側向在一般使用不超過 0.2 m/s²、特殊人群情況 0.4 m/s²。千禧橋的改造加裝了 37 組黏滯阻尼器與 52 組調諧質量阻尼器，2002 年 2 月 22 日重新開放後沒有再出現明顯振動。改造前後都需要動態試驗：前者確定要對付哪些振態，後者證明阻尼確實達到目標。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「黏滯阻尼器與調諧質量阻尼器」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Vibration of footbridges and light bridges is mostly a serviceability issue rather than a strength issue, judged by acceleration: EN 1990 Annex A2 recommends a maximum footbridge acceleration of 0.7 m/s² vertically and 0.2 m/s² laterally in normal use, 0.4 m/s² for exceptional crowds. The Millennium Bridge retrofit added 37 viscous dampers and 52 tuned mass dampers, and since reopening on 22 February 2002 it has shown no significant vibration. Dynamic tests are needed both before a retrofit, to identify the modes to treat, and after it, to prove the damping target was reached. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Viscous dampers and TMDs” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：共振加速度 a ≈ F/(2ζM)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Resonant acceleration a ≈ F/(2ζM).","failure":"常見誤解：「加大構件斷面一定是解決人行橋振動最有效的方法。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Enlarging member sections is always the most effective cure for footbridge vibration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「黏滯阻尼器與調諧質量阻尼器」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Viscous dampers and TMDs”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-33-k1","title":"舒適度準則與振動改善","titleEn":"Comfort criteria and vibration retrofit","text":"人行橋與輕量橋梁的振動多半是使用性問題而非強度問題，判斷標準是加速度：歐洲規範 EN 1990 附錄 A2 建議人行橋垂直加速度不超過 0.7 m/s²，側向在一般使用不超過 0.2 m/s²、特殊人群情況 0.4 m/s²。千禧橋的改造加裝了 37 組黏滯阻尼器與 52 組調諧質量阻尼器，2002 年 2 月 22 日重新開放後沒有再出現明顯振動。","textEn":"Vibration of footbridges and light bridges is mostly a serviceability issue rather than a strength issue, judged by acceleration: EN 1990 Annex A2 recommends a maximum footbridge acceleration of 0.7 m/s² vertically and 0.2 m/s² laterally in normal use, 0.4 m/s² for exceptional crowds. The Millennium Bridge retrofit added 37 viscous dampers and 52 tuned mass dampers, and since reopening on 22 February 2002 it has shown no significant vibration.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：加大構件斷面一定是解決人行橋振動最有效的方法。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Enlarging member sections is always the most effective cure for footbridge vibration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「舒適度準則與振動改善」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Comfort criteria and vibration retrofit\" is correct?","options":["人行橋與輕量橋梁的振動多半是使用性問題而非強度問題，判斷標準是加速度：歐洲規範 EN 1990 附錄 A2 建議人行橋垂直加速度不超過 0.7 m/s²，側向在一般使用不超過 0.2 m/s²、特殊人群情況 0.4 m/s²。","加大構件斷面一定是解決人行橋振動最有效的方法。","載重試驗通過一次，就證明橋梁永遠安全。"],"optionsEn":["Vibration of footbridges and light bridges is mostly a serviceability issue rather than a strength issue, judged by acceleration: EN 1990 Annex A2 recommends a maximum footbridge acceleration of 0.7 m/s² vertically and 0.2 m/s² laterally in normal use, 0.4 m/s² for exceptional crowds.","Enlarging member sections is always the most effective cure for footbridge vibration.","Passing one load test proves the bridge safe forever."],"answer":0,"explanation":"人行橋與輕量橋梁的振動多半是使用性問題而非強度問題，判斷標準是加速度：歐洲規範 EN 1990 附錄 A2 建議人行橋垂直加速度不超過 0.7 m/s²，側向在一般使用不超過 0.2 m/s²、特殊人群情況 0.4 m/s²。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Vibration of footbridges and light bridges is mostly a serviceability issue rather than a strength issue, judged by acceleration: EN 1990 Annex A2 recommends a maximum footbridge acceleration of 0.7 m/s² vertically and 0.2 m/s² laterally in normal use, 0.4 m/s² for exceptional crowds. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b058-v13-34","title":"舒適度準則與振動改善：定量估算","titleEn":"Comfort criteria and vibration retrofit: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「黏滯阻尼器與調諧質量阻尼器」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Viscous dampers and TMDs” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：共振加速度 a ≈ F/(2ζM)。側向等效人群力 F = 250 N、模態質量 M = 100,000 kg、ζ = 0.5%：a = 250/(2×0.005×100,000) = 0.25 m/s²，超過 0.2 m/s²；要降到 0.2 m/s² 需 ζ ≥ 250/(2×100,000×0.2) ≈ 0.63%，實務上會取更高的阻尼以涵蓋人群同步。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Resonant acceleration a ≈ F/(2ζM). With an equivalent lateral crowd force F = 250 N, modal mass M = 100,000 kg and ζ = 0.5%, a = 250/(2×0.005×100,000) = 0.25 m/s², above 0.2 m/s²; reaching 0.2 m/s² needs ζ ≥ 250/(2×100,000×0.2) ≈ 0.63%, and practice adopts much higher damping to cover crowd lock-in. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：改造後以與改造前相同的條件重做試驗（同樣的人數分級或激振頻率），比較加速度與阻尼比；阻尼器出廠前另做力—速度試驗，交接時記錄每組阻尼器的編號與位置，作為日後維護比對的基準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After a retrofit, repeat the tests under the same conditions as before (same crowd stages or excitation frequencies) and compare accelerations and damping ratios; test each damper for force and velocity before delivery, and record serial numbers and locations at handover as the baseline for later maintenance.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"共振加速度 a ≈ F/(2ζM)。側向等效人群力 F = 250 N、模態質量 M = 100,000 kg、ζ = 0.5%：a = 250/(2×0.005×100,000) = 0.25 m/s²，超過 0.2 m/s²；要降到 0.2 m/s² 需 ζ ≥ 250/(2×100,000×0.2) ≈ 0.63%，實務上會取更高的阻尼以涵蓋人群同步。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Resonant acceleration a ≈ F/(2ζM). With an equivalent lateral crowd force F = 250 N, modal mass M = 100,000 kg and ζ = 0.5%, a = 250/(2×0.005×100,000) = 0.25 m/s², above 0.2 m/s²; reaching 0.2 m/s² needs ζ ≥ 250/(2×100,000×0.2) ≈ 0.63%, and practice adopts much higher damping to cover crowd lock-in. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「舒適度準則與振動改善」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Comfort criteria and vibration retrofit\", which statement holds?","options":["只要垂直頻率避開 2 Hz，人行橋就不會有振動問題。","共振加速度 a ≈ F/(2ζM)。","只要量到最大應變，取樣率高低並不重要。"],"optionsEn":["As long as the vertical frequency avoids 2 Hz, a footbridge will have no vibration problems.","Resonant acceleration a ≈ F/(2ζM).","As long as the maximum strain is captured, sampling rate does not matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共振加速度 a ≈ F/(2ζM)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Resonant acceleration a ≈ F/(2ζM). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b058-v13-35","title":"舒適度準則與振動改善：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Comfort criteria and vibration retrofit: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「黏滯阻尼器與調諧質量阻尼器」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Viscous dampers and TMDs” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"改造後以與改造前相同的條件重做試驗（同樣的人數分級或激振頻率），比較加速度與阻尼比；阻尼器出廠前另做力—速度試驗，交接時記錄每組阻尼器的編號與位置，作為日後維護比對的基準。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After a retrofit, repeat the tests under the same conditions as before (same crowd stages or excitation frequencies) and compare accelerations and damping ratios; test each damper for force and velocity before delivery, and record serial numbers and locations at handover as the baseline for later maintenance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：振動改善設計應由設計者、阻尼器供應商與試驗單位共同確認目標振態與目標阻尼，並把改造後的驗證試驗列為重新開放的停留點，由業主核准後才開放通行。","observationEn":"Site practice: The designer, damper supplier and test team should jointly confirm target modes and target damping, and the post-retrofit verification test should be a hold point for reopening, released only on the owner's approval.","failure":"注意干擾：若只針對開幕時出問題的振態加裝阻尼，未檢查其他接近步頻的振態，人群密度增加後可能換另一個振態被激發；阻尼器連接件鬆動或漏油，也會使阻尼逐年下降而無人察覺。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Damping only the mode that misbehaved at opening, without checking other modes near walking frequencies, lets another mode take over when crowds grow denser; loose damper connections or leaking units let damping fall year by year unnoticed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"改造後以與改造前相同的條件重做試驗（同樣的人數分級或激振頻率），比較加速度與阻尼比；阻尼器出廠前另做力—速度試驗，交接時記錄每組阻尼器的編號與位置，作為日後維護比對的基準。","textEn":"After a retrofit, repeat the tests under the same conditions as before (same crowd stages or excitation frequencies) and compare accelerations and damping ratios; test each damper for force and velocity before delivery, and record serial numbers and locations at handover as the baseline for later maintenance.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"振動改善設計應由設計者、阻尼器供應商與試驗單位共同確認目標振態與目標阻尼，並把改造後的驗證試驗列為重新開放的停留點，由業主核准後才開放通行。","textEn":"The designer, damper supplier and test team should jointly confirm target modes and target damping, and the post-retrofit verification test should be a hold point for reopening, released only on the owner's approval.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「舒適度準則與振動改善」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Comfort criteria and vibration retrofit\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","人行橋只要強度設計通過，就不必做人群振動試驗。","改造後以與改造前相同的條件重做試驗（同樣的人數分級或激振頻率），比較加速度與阻尼比。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","If a footbridge passes its strength design, it needs no crowd vibration test.","After a retrofit, repeat the tests under the same conditions as before (same crowd stages or excitation frequencies) and compare accelerations and damping ratios."],"answer":2,"explanation":"改造後以與改造前相同的條件重做試驗（同樣的人數分級或激振頻率），比較加速度與阻尼比；阻尼器出廠前另做力—速度試驗，交接時記錄每組阻尼器的編號與位置，作為日後維護比對的基準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After a retrofit, repeat the tests under the same conditions as before (same crowd stages or excitation frequencies) and compare accelerations and damping ratios; test each damper for force and velocity before delivery, and record serial numbers and locations at handover as the baseline for later maintenance. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b058-v13-36","title":"舒適度準則與振動改善：失效診斷","titleEn":"Comfort criteria and vibration retrofit: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「黏滯阻尼器與調諧質量阻尼器」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Viscous dampers and TMDs” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只針對開幕時出問題的振態加裝阻尼，未檢查其他接近步頻的振態，人群密度增加後可能換另一個振態被激發；阻尼器連接件鬆動或漏油，也會使阻尼逐年下降而無人察覺。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Damping only the mode that misbehaved at opening, without checking other modes near walking frequencies, lets another mode take over when crowds grow denser; loose damper connections or leaking units let damping fall year by year unnoticed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：改造前後都需要動態試驗：前者確定要對付哪些振態，後者證明阻尼確實達到目標。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Dynamic tests are needed both before a retrofit, to identify the modes to treat, and after it, to prove the damping target was reached.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「加大構件斷面一定是解決人行橋振動最有效的方法。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Enlarging member sections is always the most effective cure for footbridge vibration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只針對開幕時出問題的振態加裝阻尼，未檢查其他接近步頻的振態，人群密度增加後可能換另一個振態被激發；阻尼器連接件鬆動或漏油，也會使阻尼逐年下降而無人察覺。","textEn":"Damping only the mode that misbehaved at opening, without checking other modes near walking frequencies, lets another mode take over when crowds grow denser; loose damper connections or leaking units let damping fall year by year unnoticed.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「舒適度準則與振動改善」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Comfort criteria and vibration retrofit\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若只針對開幕時出問題的振態加裝阻尼，未檢查其他接近步頻的振態，人群密度增加後可能換另一個振態被激發；阻尼器連接件鬆動或漏油，也會使阻尼逐年下降而無人察覺。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","載重試驗通過一次，就證明橋梁永遠安全。"],"optionsEn":["Damping only the mode that misbehaved at opening, without checking other modes near walking frequencies, lets another mode take over when crowds grow denser.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Passing one load test proves the bridge safe forever."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若只針對開幕時出問題的振態加裝阻尼，未檢查其他接近步頻的振態，人群密度增加後可能換另一個振態被激發；阻尼器連接件鬆動或漏油，也會使阻尼逐年下降而無人察覺。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Damping only the mode that misbehaved at opening, without checking other modes near walking frequencies, lets another mode take over when crowds grow denser; loose damper connections or leaking units let damping fall year by year unnoticed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b058-v13-37","title":"試驗報告、重現性與基準交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Test report, repeatability and baseline handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「動態試驗基準檔」如何影響橋梁動態荷重試驗的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Dynamic-test baseline file” governs force, deformation or durability in “Dynamic bridge load testing”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"一次動態試驗的價值會延續數十年：它提供橋梁在已知載重、溫度與路面下的頻率、阻尼、動力放大與影響線，是之後健康監測、補強與重新評等的比較基準。要讓基準能被他人使用，報告必須保存原始資料、試驗車重與軸距、車速與車道、感測器位置與方向、溫度與路面狀況，並說明結果的離散度。千禧橋改造前後以同一套試驗邏輯對照，正是用試驗驗證工程成效的例子；1940 年塔科馬海峽橋通車約四個月即在風中倒塌，也提醒動力行為必須被量測而不只是假設。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「動態試驗基準檔」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A single dynamic test keeps its value for decades: it gives frequencies, damping, amplification and influence lines under known load, temperature and surface condition, the baseline for later monitoring, strengthening and re-rating. For others to use it, the report must preserve raw data, truck weights and axle spacings, speeds and lanes, sensor positions and orientations, temperature and surface condition, and state the scatter of results. Comparing the Millennium Bridge before and after its retrofit with the same test logic is an example of verifying engineering work by testing, and the Tacoma Narrows Bridge, which fell in the wind about four months after opening in 1940, is a reminder that dynamic behaviour must be measured, not merely assumed. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Dynamic-test baseline file” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：三趟重複得 DAF = 1.18、1.22、1.15：平均 1.183、標準差 0.035；95% 信賴區間半寬 = t(0.975, 2)×s/√3 = 4.303×0.035/1.732 ≈ 0.087，上限約 1.27。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Three repeat runs give DAF = 1.18, 1.22 and 1.15: mean 1.183, standard deviation 0.035; the 95% confidence half-width is t(0.975, 2)×s/√3 = 4.303×0.035/1.732 ≈ 0.087, an upper bound of about 1.27.","failure":"常見誤解：「載重試驗通過一次，就證明橋梁永遠安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Passing one load test proves the bridge safe forever.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「動態試驗基準檔」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Dynamic-test baseline file”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-37-k1","title":"試驗報告、重現性與基準交接","titleEn":"Test report, repeatability and baseline handover","text":"一次動態試驗的價值會延續數十年：它提供橋梁在已知載重、溫度與路面下的頻率、阻尼、動力放大與影響線，是之後健康監測、補強與重新評等的比較基準。要讓基準能被他人使用，報告必須保存原始資料、試驗車重與軸距、車速與車道、感測器位置與方向、溫度與路面狀況，並說明結果的離散度。","textEn":"A single dynamic test keeps its value for decades: it gives frequencies, damping, amplification and influence lines under known load, temperature and surface condition, the baseline for later monitoring, strengthening and re-rating. For others to use it, the report must preserve raw data, truck weights and axle spacings, speeds and lanes, sensor positions and orientations, temperature and surface condition, and state the scatter of results.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：載重試驗通過一次，就證明橋梁永遠安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Passing one load test proves the bridge safe forever. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「試驗報告、重現性與基準交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Test report, repeatability and baseline handover\" is correct?","options":["載重試驗通過一次，就證明橋梁永遠安全。","一次動態試驗的價值會延續數十年：它提供橋梁在已知載重、溫度與路面下的頻率、阻尼、動力放大與影響線，是之後健康監測、補強與重新評等的比較基準。","車速越快，橋梁的動力放大一定越大。"],"optionsEn":["Passing one load test proves the bridge safe forever.","A single dynamic test keeps its value for decades: it gives frequencies, damping, amplification and influence lines under known load, temperature and surface condition, the baseline for later monitoring, strengthening and re-rating.","The faster the vehicle, the larger the dynamic amplification must be."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一次動態試驗的價值會延續數十年：它提供橋梁在已知載重、溫度與路面下的頻率、阻尼、動力放大與影響線，是之後健康監測、補強與重新評等的比較基準。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A single dynamic test keeps its value for decades: it gives frequencies, damping, amplification and influence lines under known load, temperature and surface condition, the baseline for later monitoring, strengthening and re-rating. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b058-v13-38","title":"試驗報告、重現性與基準交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Test report, repeatability and baseline handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「動態試驗基準檔」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Dynamic-test baseline file” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：三趟重複得 DAF = 1.18、1.22、1.15：平均 1.183、標準差 0.035；95% 信賴區間半寬 = t(0.975, 2)×s/√3 = 4.303×0.035/1.732 ≈ 0.087，上限約 1.27。評等若採 1.27 仍低於規範的 1.33；若只做一趟，就無法評估這個離散度。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Three repeat runs give DAF = 1.18, 1.22 and 1.15: mean 1.183, standard deviation 0.035; the 95% confidence half-width is t(0.975, 2)×s/√3 = 4.303×0.035/1.732 ≈ 0.087, an upper bound of about 1.27. Rating with 1.27 still stays below the code's 1.33; a single run could not reveal this scatter at all. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：交接前由第三方抽取數趟原始資料，依報告記載的處理參數重算峰值、動力放大與頻率，確認可以重現；檢查報告是否附有試驗車秤重單、儀器校正證書與試驗日誌，並確認資料格式可被業主的監測系統讀取。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before handover, have a third party take several raw runs and recompute peaks, amplification and frequencies with the processing parameters in the report to confirm reproducibility; check that weighbridge tickets, calibration certificates and the test log are attached and that the data format can be read by the owner's monitoring system.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"三趟重複得 DAF = 1.18、1.22、1.15：平均 1.183、標準差 0.035；95% 信賴區間半寬 = t(0.975, 2)×s/√3 = 4.303×0.035/1.732 ≈ 0.087，上限約 1.27。評等若採 1.27 仍低於規範的 1.33；若只做一趟，就無法評估這個離散度。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Three repeat runs give DAF = 1.18, 1.22 and 1.15: mean 1.183, standard deviation 0.035; the 95% confidence half-width is t(0.975, 2)×s/√3 = 4.303×0.035/1.732 ≈ 0.087, an upper bound of about 1.27. Rating with 1.27 still stays below the code's 1.33; a single run could not reveal this scatter at all. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「試驗報告、重現性與基準交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Test report, repeatability and baseline handover\", which statement holds?","options":["載重試驗用的車越重，得到的結論就越可靠。","動態試驗只要讓卡車以最高速通過一次就夠了。","三趟重複得 DAF = 1.18、1.22、1.15：平均 1.183、標準差 0.035。"],"optionsEn":["The heavier the test vehicle, the more reliable the conclusions.","A dynamic test only needs one pass of the truck at top speed.","Three repeat runs give DAF = 1.18, 1.22 and 1.15: mean 1.183, standard deviation 0.035."],"answer":2,"explanation":"三趟重複得 DAF = 1.18、1.22、1.15：平均 1.183、標準差 0.035；95% 信賴區間半寬 = t(0.975, 2)×s/√3 = 4.303×0.035/1.732 ≈ 0.087，上限約 1.27。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Three repeat runs give DAF = 1.18, 1.22 and 1.15: mean 1.183, standard deviation 0.035; the 95% confidence half-width is t(0.975, 2)×s/√3 = 4.303×0.035/1.732 ≈ 0.087, an upper bound of about 1.27. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b058-v13-39","title":"試驗報告、重現性與基準交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Test report, repeatability and baseline handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「動態試驗基準檔」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Dynamic-test baseline file” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"交接前由第三方抽取數趟原始資料，依報告記載的處理參數重算峰值、動力放大與頻率，確認可以重現；檢查報告是否附有試驗車秤重單、儀器校正證書與試驗日誌，並確認資料格式可被業主的監測系統讀取。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before handover, have a third party take several raw runs and recompute peaks, amplification and frequencies with the processing parameters in the report to confirm reproducibility; check that weighbridge tickets, calibration certificates and the test log are attached and that the data format can be read by the owner's monitoring system. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：業主應把動態試驗資料納入橋梁管理系統，訂定重新試驗的觸發條件（重大補強、事故、評等變更、伸縮縫更換），並要求後續試驗盡量沿用相同的量測點與試驗車配置，以便直接比較。","observationEn":"Site practice: The owner should load dynamic-test data into the bridge management system, define triggers for retesting (major strengthening, accidents, rating changes, joint replacement), and require later tests to reuse the same gauge locations and truck configuration wherever possible so results compare directly.","failure":"注意干擾：若報告只留下結論數字，十年後橋梁補強或改建時，工程師無法判斷頻率變化是結構改變還是試驗方法不同；試驗車重與溫度紀錄缺漏，則讓前後兩次試驗無法比較。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the report keeps only conclusions, engineers strengthening or rebuilding the bridge ten years later cannot tell whether a frequency change reflects the structure or a different test method; missing truck weights or temperatures make the two tests incomparable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"交接前由第三方抽取數趟原始資料，依報告記載的處理參數重算峰值、動力放大與頻率，確認可以重現；檢查報告是否附有試驗車秤重單、儀器校正證書與試驗日誌，並確認資料格式可被業主的監測系統讀取。","textEn":"Before handover, have a third party take several raw runs and recompute peaks, amplification and frequencies with the processing parameters in the report to confirm reproducibility; check that weighbridge tickets, calibration certificates and the test log are attached and that the data format can be read by the owner's monitoring system.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"業主應把動態試驗資料納入橋梁管理系統，訂定重新試驗的觸發條件（重大補強、事故、評等變更、伸縮縫更換），並要求後續試驗盡量沿用相同的量測點與試驗車配置，以便直接比較。","textEn":"The owner should load dynamic-test data into the bridge management system, define triggers for retesting (major strengthening, accidents, rating changes, joint replacement), and require later tests to reuse the same gauge locations and truck configuration wherever possible so results compare directly.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「試驗報告、重現性與基準交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Test report, repeatability and baseline handover\"?","options":["交接前由第三方抽取數趟原始資料，依報告記載的處理參數重算峰值、動力放大與頻率，確認可以重現。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","實測頻率比模型高，就代表橋梁沒有任何問題。"],"optionsEn":["Before handover, have a third party take several raw runs and recompute peaks, amplification and frequencies with the processing parameters in the report to confirm reproducibility.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A measured frequency higher than the model means the bridge has no problems."],"answer":0,"explanation":"交接前由第三方抽取數趟原始資料，依報告記載的處理參數重算峰值、動力放大與頻率，確認可以重現；檢查報告是否附有試驗車秤重單、儀器校正證書與試驗日誌，並確認資料格式可被業主的監測系統讀取。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before handover, have a third party take several raw runs and recompute peaks, amplification and frequencies with the processing parameters in the report to confirm reproducibility; check that weighbridge tickets, calibration certificates and the test log are attached and that the data format can be read by the owner's monitoring system. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b058-v13-40","title":"試驗報告、重現性與基準交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Test report, repeatability and baseline handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b058-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「動態試驗基準檔」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Dynamic-test baseline file” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若報告只留下結論數字，十年後橋梁補強或改建時，工程師無法判斷頻率變化是結構改變還是試驗方法不同；試驗車重與溫度紀錄缺漏，則讓前後兩次試驗無法比較。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the report keeps only conclusions, engineers strengthening or rebuilding the bridge ten years later cannot tell whether a frequency change reflects the structure or a different test method; missing truck weights or temperatures make the two tests incomparable. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：千禧橋改造前後以同一套試驗邏輯對照，正是用試驗驗證工程成效的例子；1940 年塔科馬海峽橋通車約四個月即在風中倒塌，也提醒動力行為必須被量測而不只是假設。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Comparing the Millennium Bridge before and after its retrofit with the same test logic is an example of verifying engineering work by testing, and the Tacoma Narrows Bridge, which fell in the wind about four months after opening in 1940, is a reminder that dynamic behaviour must be measured, not merely assumed.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「載重試驗通過一次，就證明橋梁永遠安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Passing one load test proves the bridge safe forever.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b058-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若報告只留下結論數字，十年後橋梁補強或改建時，工程師無法判斷頻率變化是結構改變還是試驗方法不同；試驗車重與溫度紀錄缺漏，則讓前後兩次試驗無法比較。","textEn":"If the report keeps only conclusions, engineers strengthening or rebuilding the bridge ten years later cannot tell whether a frequency change reflects the structure or a different test method; missing truck weights or temperatures make the two tests incomparable.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b058-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「試驗報告、重現性與基準交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Test report, repeatability and baseline handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若報告只留下結論數字，十年後橋梁補強或改建時，工程師無法判斷頻率變化是結構改變還是試驗方法不同；試驗車重與溫度紀錄缺漏，則讓前後兩次試驗無法比較。","車速越快，橋梁的動力放大一定越大。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","If the report keeps only conclusions, engineers strengthening or rebuilding the bridge ten years later cannot tell whether a frequency change reflects the structure or a different test method.","The faster the vehicle, the larger the dynamic amplification must be."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若報告只留下結論數字，十年後橋梁補強或改建時，工程師無法判斷頻率變化是結構改變還是試驗方法不同；試驗車重與溫度紀錄缺漏，則讓前後兩次試驗無法比較。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the report keeps only conclusions, engineers strengthening or rebuilding the bridge ten years later cannot tell whether a frequency change reflects the structure or a different test method; missing truck weights or temperatures make the two tests incomparable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-trb-ec257-load-testing","v13s-arup-millennium-bridge","v13s-wsdot-tnb-history","v13s-wiki-millennium-bridge","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
